      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbnxop4-3d1x",
      "title": "Thousands of rare wildflowers rescued from eroding Scottish coast",
      "description": "<p>Conservationists relocate 3,400 one-flowered wintergreens, a species estimated to have lost more than half its UK population in the past 50 years</p><p>Thousands of one of Britain’s rarest wildflowers have been moved to safety from an eroding Scottish shoreline where they were at risk of falling into the sea.</p><p>Conservationists rescued 3,400 one-flowered wintergreen plants at Culbin Forest in Moray, in an effort to protect a species estimated to have lost more than half its UK population in the past 50 years.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/11/one-flowered-wintergreen-rescue-eroding-coast-scotland\">Continue reading...</a>",
