      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbnxop2-36ow",
      "title": "Fresh concerns raised over Gaza doctor held by Israel for 23 months without charge",
      "description": "<p>Independent Israeli professor says Hussam Abu Safiya’s life will be at risk until he receives proper medical treatment</p><p>An independent professor who reviewed the medical records of a prominent Gaza doctor held in an Israeli prison without charge for nearly 23 months has raised serious concerns about his health.</p><p>Hussam Abu Safiya was detained at work on 27 December 2024 and later held in solitary confinement at Rakefet, a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/nov/08/israel-underground-jail-rakefet-palestinians-gaza-detainees\">notorious underground</a> prison.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/11/fresh-concerns-over-gaza-doctor-held-by-israel\">Continue reading...</a>",
