      "easySummary": "<p><strong>Exclusive</strong>: Jillian Segal suggested ‘transferring’ powers in updated report released a fortnight ago but government sources note media regulator already exists</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Albanese government won’t follow a suggestion by the antisemitism envoy to scrap the ABC and SBS ombudsmen and replace them with an external oversight body.</p><p>In a list of updated priorities released last month, Segal proposed an <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/oct/30/jillian-segal-antisemitism-envoy-plan-report-priorities-ntwnfb\">“external independent ombudsman”</a> to monitor ABC and SBS coverage of the war in Gaza and to ensure publicly funded broadcasters were “held accountable to their own stated standards of accuracy and impartiality”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/nov/11/labor-abc-sbs-ombudsmen-antisemitism-envoy-gaza-coverage-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian World, this report highlights developments in World News.\n\nHeadline: \"Labor won’t scrap ABC and SBS ombudsmen in favour of external body as suggested by antisemitism envoy\"\n\n<p><strong>Exclusive</strong>: Jillian Segal suggested ‘transferring’ powers in updated report released a fortnight ago but government sources note media regulator already exists</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Albanese government won’t follow a suggestion by the antisemitism envoy to scrap the ABC and SBS ombudsmen and replace them with an external oversight body.</p><p>In a list of updated priorities released last month, Segal proposed an <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/oct/30/jillian-segal-antisemitism-envoy-plan-report-priorities-ntwnfb\">“external independent ombudsman”</a> to monitor ABC and SBS coverage of the war in Gaza and to ensure publicly funded broadcasters were “held accountable to their own stated standards of accuracy and impartiality”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/nov/11/labor-abc-sbs-ombudsmen-antisemitism-envoy-gaza-coverage-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
