    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbmsbn9-oeuh",
      "title": "Two white students at University of Mississippi make monkey gestures in Ring video",
      "description": "<p>Women are reportedly upstairs neighbors of three Black students, including one who uploaded video to TikTok</p><p>Two white students at the University of Mississippi were captured making offensive monkey gestures in a widely panned Ring video that has prompted a school <a href=\"https://t.e2ma.net/message/sqez5j/o3p5id2d\">investigation</a>.</p><p>On Saturday, freshman Jakiyra Metcalf <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@jakiyrametcalf_/video/7705269758194666765?_r=1&amp;_t=ZP-9BIr8MvWTM7\">uploaded</a> the surveillance clip from her apartment door to TikTok, showing one woman thumping her chest and babbling like a monkey. Another woman jumped into the camera’s view and mimicked the primate noises.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/10/university-of-mississippi-white-students-monkey-gestures\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/10/university-of-mississippi-white-students-monkey-gestures",
