    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbmsbn7-nlkb",
      "title": "‘No one is in charge’: social care system in England in chaos, Louise Casey to say",
      "description": "<p>Head of major review into adult social care will say that governments have been ‘asleep at the wheel’ of vital system</p><p>Successive governments in England have been “asleep at the wheel” on social care, leaving the system to grow as a chaotic patchwork of local services with no clear vision, Louise Casey, the head of the social care commission, is to warn.</p><p>Lady Casey, who is preparing proposals for a big <a href=\"https://caseycommission.co.uk/\">review of adult social care</a>, will say the result is that in effect “no one is in charge” of a system that provides vital services for millions of vulnerable people.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/11/louise-casey-england-social-care-system\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/11/louise-casey-england-social-care-system",
