    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbmsbn7-7pjf",
      "title": "Disabled people in England ‘have to wait up to two years for wheelchairs’",
      "description": "<p>Ombudsman’s report says delays have profound consequences and limit users’ ability to lead independent lives</p><p>Disabled people are having to wait up to two years to get a wheelchair because of delays involving NHS bodies and private firms that make them.</p><p>The situation is revealed in a report by the parliamentary and health service ombudsman for England, Paula Sussex, who said hold-ups were having profound consequences and limiting wheelchair users’ ability to lead independent lives.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/11/disabled-people-in-england-have-to-wait-up-to-two-years-for-wheelchairs\">Continue reading...</a>",
