    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbmsbn8-e3nc",
      "title": "US prosecutors charge Iranian operative allegedly responsible for UK air force base attack",
      "description": "<p>New indictment claims Mohammad Dawood al-Saadi, a dual Iranian and Iraqi national, plotted while in US custody</p><p>US federal prosecutors have said that an Iranian operative jailed in New York was responsible for the foiled attack on a UK air force base where American B-1 bombers were stationed.</p><p>A new indictment alleged that Mohammad Dawood al-Saadi, a dual Iranian and Iraqi national, plotted while in custody and then transmitted plans – using coded messages in calls to his family – to two co-conspirators to buy large quantities of chemicals that could be used as explosives in an attack on the RAF Fairford base in September.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/10/prosecutors-charge-iranian-operative-uk-air-force-attack\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/10/prosecutors-charge-iranian-operative-uk-air-force-attack",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/10/prosecutors-charge-iranian-operative-uk-air-force-attack",
      "publisherId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian World",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardianworld",
