    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mwbms7dz-i786",
      "title": "Will Joseph poised to audition for leading role against Japan in Feyi-Waboso’s absence",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>England require back-line reshuffle after several injuries</p></li><li><p>Kevin Sinfield says collaboration with clubs will be key</p></li></ul><p>England need to find a talented understudy for their <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/09/england-fresh-injury-woe-feyi-waboso-tom-curry-out-nations-championship\">injured star wing Manny Feyi-Waboso</a>, and are poised to invite Gloucester’s Will Joseph to audition for a ­leading role against Japan on Saturday. The latter was a travelling reserve for last ­weekend’s Australia game and appears set for a Test recall four years after being given his debut by the current Brave ­Blossoms head coach, Eddie Jones.</p><p>The 24-year-old Joseph, whose brother Jonathan was a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2017/feb/10/jonathan-joseph-england-wales-six-nations-fans\">regular in England’s midfield for years</a>, has been in outstanding club form and, as things stand, seems likely to ­feature in some capacity with injuries ­forcing Steve Borthwick to reconsider the backline blend that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/08/england-australia-nations-championship-rugby-union-match-report\">prospered against the Wallabies</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/10/rugby-union-england-japan-nations-championship-will-joseph\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/10/rugby-union-england-japan-nations-championship-will-joseph",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/10/rugby-union-england-japan-nations-championship-will-joseph",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Sport",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardiansport",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Sports",
      "currentAffairsCategory": "Sports",
      "publishDate": "2026-11-10T18:41:49.000Z",
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T18:41:49.000Z",
      "firstSeenAt": "2026-11-11T04:40:40.306Z",
      "lastCheckedAt": "2026-11-11T05:12:50.723Z",
      "contentHash": "27a32f86de351e15",
      "isUpdate": false,
      "readingTimeMinutes": 5,
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/6ede15e102105fb6d77d8cc1aed5763d7f7293eb/0_163_3401_2720/master/3401.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=9c9f384fc8f68027d41c9aa3fcaa84ed&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "originalImageUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/6ede15e102105fb6d77d8cc1aed5763d7f7293eb/0_163_3401_2720/master/3401.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=9c9f384fc8f68027d41c9aa3fcaa84ed&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "imageSource": "publisher",
      "imageType": "photo",
      "imageCaption": "Official photograph from The Guardian Sport for \"Will Joseph poised to audition for leading role against Japan in Feyi-Waboso’s absence\"",
      "imageAttribution": "Source: The Guardian Sport",
      "imageValidationStatus": "valid",
      "quickSummary": [
        "Official verified dispatch from The Guardian Sport: \"Will Joseph poised to audition for leading role against Japan in Feyi-Waboso’s absence\".",
        "Key Context: <ul><li><p>England require back-line reshuffle after several injuries</p></li><li><p>Kevin Sinfield says collaboration with clubs will be key</p></li></ul><p>England need to find a talented understudy.",
        "Categorized under Sports for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by The Guardian Sport. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "<ul><li><p>England require back-line reshuffle after several injuries</p></li><li><p>Kevin Sinfield says collaboration with clubs will be key</p></li></ul><p>England need to find a talented understudy for their <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/09/england-fresh-injury-woe-feyi-waboso-tom-curry-out-nations-championship\">injured star wing Manny Feyi-Waboso</a>, and are poised to invite Gloucester’s Will Joseph to audition for a ­leading role against Japan on Saturday. The latter was a travelling reserve for last ­weekend’s Australia game and appears set for a Test recall four years after being given his debut by the current Brave ­Blossoms head coach, Eddie Jones.</p><p>The 24-year-old Joseph, whose brother Jonathan was a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2017/feb/10/jonathan-joseph-england-wales-six-nations-fans\">regular in England’s midfield for years</a>, has been in outstanding club form and, as things stand, seems likely to ­feature in some capacity with injuries ­forcing Steve Borthwick to reconsider the backline blend that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/08/england-australia-nations-championship-rugby-union-match-report\">prospered against the Wallabies</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/10/rugby-union-england-japan-nations-championship-will-joseph\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian Sport, this report highlights developments in Sports.\n\nHeadline: \"Will Joseph poised to audition for leading role against Japan in Feyi-Waboso’s absence\"\n\n<ul><li><p>England require back-line reshuffle after several injuries</p></li><li><p>Kevin Sinfield says collaboration with clubs will be key</p></li></ul><p>England need to find a talented understudy for their <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/09/england-fresh-injury-woe-feyi-waboso-tom-curry-out-nations-championship\">injured star wing Manny Feyi-Waboso</a>, and are poised to invite Gloucester’s Will Joseph to audition for a ­leading role against Japan on Saturday. The latter was a travelling reserve for last ­weekend’s Australia game and appears set for a Test recall four years after being given his debut by the current Brave ­Blossoms head coach, Eddie Jones.</p><p>The 24-year-old Joseph, whose brother Jonathan was a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2017/feb/10/jonathan-joseph-england-wales-six-nations-fans\">regular in England’s midfield for years</a>, has been in outstanding club form and, as things stand, seems likely to ­feature in some capacity with injuries ­forcing Steve Borthwick to reconsider the backline blend that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/08/england-australia-nations-championship-rugby-union-match-report\">prospered against the Wallabies</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/10/rugby-union-england-japan-nations-championship-will-joseph\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
