      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbmsbn4-1nss",
      "title": "Russian naval aggression prompts new defensive initiative with ‘beer-drinking nations’",
      "description": "<p>New alliance with the Netherlands and Baltic and Nordic countries comes in response to 41% increase in Russian naval activity around UK</p><p>Russian naval activity around the UK has increased by 41% in the first nine months of the year, a British defence minister has said, as the Royal Navy announced plans to step up a 10-country maritime defensive effort in response.</p><p>Luke Pollard, the minister for defence readiness, described the figure as “a huge increase”, justifying a new drone and warship initiative from “the alliance of beer-drinking nations” – the UK, the Netherlands and the Baltic and Nordic countries.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/10/russian-naval-aggression-defensive-initiative-beer-drinking-nations\">Continue reading...</a>",
