      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mwbms7dz-jg8m",
      "title": "F1 presses ahead with plan to hold season finale in Middle East despite safety concerns",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Imola stood down as back-up plan to finish the year</p></li><li><p>Qatar and Abu Dhabi races set to go ahead as planned</p></li></ul><p>Imola has been stood down as a back-up plan for the Formula One season finale as the sport pushes ahead with its scheduled Middle East races.</p><p>The Italian venue, 20 miles from Bologna, was lined up to replace Abu Dhabi as the final race <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/03/qatar-abu-dhabi-grands-prix-go-ahead-middle-east-conflict-formula-one-chief-domenicali\">amid concern over the ongoing conflict</a> in the region.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/10/f1-season-finale-middle-east-conflict-formula-one-abu-dhabi-imola-qatar\">Continue reading...</a>",
