      "description": "<ul><li><p>‘We weren’t aware anything was taken on the field’</p></li><li><p>CA: no ‘compelling reason’ to establish new inquiry</p></li></ul><p>Mitchell Starc has denied claims made in Usman Khawaja’s new book that more than the three players suspended for ball tampering had knowledge of the sandpaper plan in South Africa in 2018.</p><p>Starc became the first of the Australia bowling group who played in the 2018 Cape Town Test to speak out following the publication of Khawaja’s book on Tuesday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/10/cricket-australia-rules-out-reopening-ball-tampering-investigation-usman-khawaja-book\">Continue reading...</a>",
