      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mwbms7dy-t8tw",
      "title": "Crystal Palace could avoid significant compensation if Pierre Sage rejoins Lens",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Sage’s exit from Premier League club still not confirmed</p></li><li><p>Manager’s potential return to France could benefit Palace</p></li></ul><p>Crystal Palace could avoid paying Pierre Sage significant compensation if he is reappointed by his former club, Lens, with the manager’s departure from Selhurst Park yet to be confirmed.</p><p>The decision to sack Sage was made on Sunday evening after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/08/crystal-palace-liverpool-premier-league-match-report\">Palace slumped to a 3-1 defeat against Liverpool</a>. It was their fourth successive loss in the Premier League and left them bottom of the table for the first time since 2017.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/10/pierre-sage-crystal-palace-premier-league-lens\">Continue reading...</a>",
