      "easySummary": "Scientists have discovered a remarkably preserved 450-million-year-old fossil containing soft tissues from an ancient starfish relative, revealing unexpected details about marine life more than 200 million years before dinosaurs existed. Found in a museum collection, the extraordinarily rare specimen offers new clues about how Earth&#039;s earliest reef animals fed, survived, and evolved.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"Paleontologists discover “one-in-a-million” fossil with 450-million-year-old soft tissue\"\n\nScientists have discovered a remarkably preserved 450-million-year-old fossil containing soft tissues from an ancient starfish relative, revealing unexpected details about marine life more than 200 million years before dinosaurs existed. Found in a museum collection, the extraordinarily rare specimen offers new clues about how Earth&#039;s earliest reef animals fed, survived, and evolved.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
