      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mwbms7e4-73n8",
      "title": "Sisters in Sweat: how a former Spurs player got 20,000 Indian women into sport",
      "description": "<p>A dinner-party question, a Sunday kickabout and an idea that snowballed. Nine years on, Tanvie Hans and Swetha Subbiah have taken sporting sisterhood to 10 cities</p><p>On a breezy evening in 2017, as conversations flowed and so did the drinks at a dinner party, Tanvie Hans was asked an all-too-familiar question at the table: “Hey, can you teach me how to play football?”</p><p>For the Indian-born British footballer, who played professionally in England, it was an easy yes.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/10/sisters-in-sweat-indian-women-sport-moving-the-goalposts\">Continue reading...</a>",
