    {
      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mwbmsbt5-mzo9",
      "title": "Slight fall in carbon emissions from fossil fuels as Iran war drives renewables push",
      "description": "<p>However, authors of a comprehensive assessment to be presented at Cop31 warn talk of a global turnaround premature</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/live/2026/nov/10/cop31-live-fossil-fuel-carbon-emissions-climate-crisis-latest-news-updates\">Cop31 live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Soaring <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/02/nine-of-world-biggest-oil-firms-95bn-profit-third-quarter-iran-war\">oil and gas prices</a> following the war in Iran have encouraged people to look beyond fossil fuels, leading to an easing of climate-damaging carbon emissions this year.</p><p>Carbon dioxide from oil, gas and coal is forecast to flatline for 2026, based on data from the year so far, according to a <a href=\"https://essd.copernicus.org/preprints/essd-2026-895\">comprehensive assessment by scientists</a>. Emissions from burning oil alone will drop by 2% as drivers economise on fuel use and flock to electric vehicles instead.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/10/slight-fall-in-carbon-emissions-from-fossil-fuels-as-iran-war-drives-renewables-push\">Continue reading...</a>",
