    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mwbms7e9-cm05",
      "title": "Bunny Shaw shines again for five-star Manchester City – Women’s Football Weekly",
      "description": "<p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/faye-carruthers\">Faye Carruthers</a> is joined by <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/suzywrack.bsky.social\">Suzanne Wrack</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sophie-downey\">Sophie Downey</a> and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/marva-kreel\">Marva Kreel</a> to discuss the weekend’s WSL action</p><p>On the podcast today: It is a five-star performance from Manchester City as Bunny Shaw shines again, but a frustrating afternoon for Chelsea as they are held to a draw by Everton.</p><p>Plus Arsenal would be in big trouble without Alessia Russo as her two goals help Arsenal earn three much needed points against Liverpool. Meanwhile, Beth England bagged a late winner for Crystal Palace, and there are wins for Spurs and London City Lionesses.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/audio/2026/nov/10/bunny-shaw-shines-again-for-five-star-manchester-city-womens-football-weekly\">Continue reading...</a>",
