      "easySummary": "<p>Former prime minister faces death penalty upon return after being sentenced in absentia over deaths in 2024 uprising</p><p>Sheikh Hasina is “confident” she will return to Bangladesh in December, according to exiled members of her party, after the disgraced former prime minister applied for a new passport this week.</p><p>Hasina has been living in self-imposed exile since August 2024 when she was toppled from power by a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/26/bangladesh-student-protests-mass-movement-against-dictator\">mass uprising</a> against her authoritarian rule. She crossed the border to India, where she has since been allowed to live freely in Delhi.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/disgraced-former-leader-sheikh-hasina-plans-return-to-bangladesh-after-two-years-in-exile\">Continue reading...</a>",
