    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mwbms7e4-0dar",
      "title": "Manchester City’s Kerstin Casparij: ‘I love football – but it takes over your life’",
      "description": "<p>Dutch full-back on relief of winning the Double and needing a ‘sense of normality’ while in the spotlight</p><p>Kerstin Casparij loves football, especially Champions League nights under the lights, but perspective is important too. “I would say football is my most important secondary thing in life, and I’ve found that such a refreshing way of looking at it,” she says before Manchester City’s trip to Milan to face Inter on Tuesday.</p><p>“It is so important to me and I love it so much and if I lose I’m going to have a terrible day, but my family’s healthy, my friends are healthy, I am, and I don’t have to worry about anything; I don’t have to worry about getting the food on the table. Being able to see things from that perspective makes it so much easier to stay the person I’ve always been.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/nov/10/manchester-citys-kerstin-casparij-i-love-football-but-it-takes-over-your-life\">Continue reading...</a>",
