      "title": "High fossil fuel prices spread inflation ‘like a cancer’, UN climate chief tells Cop31",
      "description": "<p>Simon Stiell makes opening address at summit in Turkey, where talks are under way about speeding up shift to electrification</p><p>A global fossil fuel price crisis is “spreading inflation like a cancer” around the planet, the UN’s climate chief, Simon Stiell, told the opening plenary of critical UN climate talks in Turkey.</p><p>Stiell joined Cop31 hosts Turkey and Australia, which is leading the negotiations, in promoting renewable energy and a new electrification goal as an optimistic alternative to a planet still tied to oil, coal and gas.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/09/high-fossil-fuel-prices-spread-inflation-like-cancer-cop31egotiator-tells-cop31\">Continue reading...</a>",
