      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mwbmsbt6-f5fy",
      "title": "Climate always comes second: are green issues slipping down Burnham’s agenda?",
      "description": "<p>Prime minister says he’s committed to meeting climate targets, but some believe his actions suggest otherwise</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/08/labour-cut-ev-target-car-industry-despite-climate-concerns\">Labour expected to cut EV targets for car industry despite MPs’ climate concerns</a></p></li></ul><p>Andy Burnham insists he is committed to the green transition, but his MPs worry that in decision after decision, he is showing that other priorities come first.</p><p>“Our changing climate is a major concern for many Britons, not least because we have just emerged from <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/01/summer-2026-uk-hottest-on-record-provisional-met-office-data\">our hottest summer on record</a>,” the prime minister <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/sep/17/andy-burnham-climate-crisis-funding-peoples-power-projects\">wrote in the Guardian</a> in September.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/08/andy-burnham-uk-climate-crisis-rosebank-jackdaw\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/08/andy-burnham-uk-climate-crisis-rosebank-jackdaw",
