      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbmsbmz-rgis",
      "title": "Collision of two trains in Egypt kills at least seven",
      "description": "<p>President orders prompt investigation after one train derails in collision in al-Ayyat about 50km from Cairo</p><p>Seven people were killed and at least 125 injured when two trains collided on Sunday south of the Egyptian capital, Cairo, officials said.</p><p>The crash occurred in al-Ayyat district in Giza province, about 50km (30 miles) south of Cairo, when a train travelling to Fayoum province crashed into the rear of a train heading to the southern province of Aswan, according to the transport ministry.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/08/egypt-two-trains-deadly-collision\">Continue reading...</a>",
