      "easySummary": "<p>See My World, an event highlighting the pan-African thought via film, poetry and dance, builds on momentum sparked by local activists and creatives</p><p>African philosophies including exploring how lessons from the past can shape the present and near future have inspired a film festival coming to Manchester.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/see-my-world-film-festival-tickets-2000609164867\">See My World</a>, a day dedicated to independent creators from across the African diaspora in the north of England, will take place at the Contact theatre on 21 November.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/nov/08/african-philosophies-see-my-world-film-festival-manchester\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian World, this report highlights developments in World News.\n\nHeadline: \"How African philosophies inspired a new approach to staging film festivals in Manchester\"\n\n<p>See My World, an event highlighting the pan-African thought via film, poetry and dance, builds on momentum sparked by local activists and creatives</p><p>African philosophies including exploring how lessons from the past can shape the present and near future have inspired a film festival coming to Manchester.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/see-my-world-film-festival-tickets-2000609164867\">See My World</a>, a day dedicated to independent creators from across the African diaspora in the north of England, will take place at the Contact theatre on 21 November.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/nov/08/african-philosophies-see-my-world-film-festival-manchester\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
