      "id": "art-sciencedaily-mwbms940-swd6",
      "title": "A nuclear blast could save Earth from an asteroid, but there&#039;s a catch",
      "description": "A nuclear explosion might save Earth from a deadly asteroid, but new research suggests that hitting the wrong side could make the difference between success and disaster. Scientists found that an asteroid&#039;s irregular shape can dramatically affect how it responds to an X-ray blast, with deflection effectiveness varying nearly fivefold depending on the angle.",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261106174532.htm",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261106174532.htm",
