      "easySummary": "A surprising new study suggests that a stronger flu shot could offer older adults significantly greater protection against Alzheimer&#039;s disease. Researchers at UTHealth Houston analyzed nearly 200,000 adults ages 65 and older and found that those who received a high-dose influenza vaccine had a nearly 55% lower risk of developing Alzheimer&#039;s, compared with a 40% reduction previously associated with the standard-dose vaccine.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"Stronger flu shot linked to nearly 55% lower Alzheimer&#039;s risk\"\n\nA surprising new study suggests that a stronger flu shot could offer older adults significantly greater protection against Alzheimer&#039;s disease. Researchers at UTHealth Houston analyzed nearly 200,000 adults ages 65 and older and found that those who received a high-dose influenza vaccine had a nearly 55% lower risk of developing Alzheimer&#039;s, compared with a 40% reduction previously associated with the standard-dose vaccine.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
