      "id": "art-guardian_world-mwbmsbn2-y89k",
      "title": "New Zealand election coalition talks will likely take weeks – as it happened",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>This blog is closed, you can <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/07/new-zealand-election-too-close-to-call-vote-count\">read our report on the New Zealand election here</a></p></li></ul><p>Another update here with <strong>8% of the vote counted</strong>. <br> <br> <strong>National on 31.2%, Labour 28.4%, the Greens 12.9%, Act 11.2%, NZ First 9.6%, Opportunity 5.7% and Te Pāti Māori 0.4%.</strong></p><p>On these numbers, we would have a right bloc coalition back in power. <em>Long way to go</em>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/07/nz-general-election-2026-live-updates-results-new-zealand-polls\">Continue reading...</a>",
