      "id": "art-mongabay-mwbms9at-k4nq",
      "title": "These divers are killing a beautiful coral to save Brazil’s marine life",
      "description": "RIO DE JANEIRO — Beneath the surface of Brazil’s coastal waters, a silent invasion is transforming marine ecosystems. Sun coral (Tubastraea coccinea and Tubastraea tagusensis), an invasive coral native to the Indo-Pacific, is spreading along Brazil’s coastline, threatening native species. First seen in Brazil in the 1980s, attached to an offshore oil platform in Rio [&#8230;]",
