      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mwbms7ea-iktj",
      "title": "Chess: Magnus Carlsen returns for Budapest battle before Sindarov targets classical crown",
      "description": "<p>The Norwegian, 35, has set up a training camp in Spain to prepare for the Budapest Total Chess pilot</p><p>November will be an important month for global chess, with the Total World Championship pilot, combining fast classical, rapid and blitz segments due in Budapest from 10-20 November. This will be followed by the Gukesh Dommaraju v Javokhir Sindarov Fide World Championship match in Geneva between 24 November and 12 December, featuring 14 games of classical chess ­followed, if needed, by rapid and blitz tie-breaks.</p><p>The traditional London Classic at the Novotel West in Hammersmith will also start on 24 November and will continue until 7 December.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/06/chess-magnus-carlsen-returns-for-budapest-battle-before-sindarov-targets-classical-crown\">Continue reading...</a>",
