      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mwbmsbta-qaoz",
      "title": "‘No one cares about the little guy’: plastic nurdles still washing ashore in Sri Lanka five years after toxic spill",
      "description": "<p>A stricken container ship shed tonnes of the tiny pellets on the west coast in May 2021. Today, locals are counting the cost to marine life and livelihoods</p><p>On the beach in Pamunugama, on Sri Lanka’s west coast, women in uniform work under the scorching sun. They sift through rubbish washed ashore, searching among the usual litter for something much smaller: tiny plastic pellets.</p><p>Five years ago, in May 2021, this same beach was swamped with pellets as smoke rose over the Indian Ocean.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/05/no-one-cares-about-the-little-guy-sri-lankas-fishers-still-reeling-from-2021-toxic-plastic-spill\">Continue reading...</a>",
