      "id": "art-sciencedaily-mwbms944-5bnr",
      "title": "NASA is racing against time to save the Hubble Space Telescope",
      "description": "NASA is exploring a daring plan to save the legendary Hubble Space Telescope from its eventual fiery plunge into Earth&#039;s atmosphere. After more than 35 years of groundbreaking discoveries, Hubble is slowly losing altitude, and without intervention, it could fall back to Earth as early as 2033 or 2034. To keep the iconic observatory operating, NASA is asking private space companies to propose innovative ways to boost Hubble into a higher orbit, upgrade its capabilities, or safely dispose of it when its mission finally ends.",
