      "title": "SLAC scientists find conclusive proof of a mysterious third type of magnetism",
      "description": "For nearly 90 years, scientists believed magnetism fell into just two categories, but researchers have now confirmed a remarkable third type called altermagnetism. Using specialized X-rays, they uncovered a unique magnetic signature that proves these materials behave differently from conventional magnets. Altermagnets combine stability with the ability to efficiently carry information, potentially overcoming major limitations in today&#039;s electronics. The discovery could lead to faster computers, more efficient data centers, and breakthroughs in quantum technology.",
