      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"A hidden star is plowing through Betelgeuse’s atmosphere, new evidence suggests\"\n\nSomething mysterious is disturbing Betelgeuse, and astronomers believe they have identified the culprit: a hidden companion star called Siwarha. New radio observations reveal that the smaller star may be plowing through Betelgeuse’s enormous atmosphere, creating disturbances that subtly stretch and distort the red supergiant’s shape.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
