      "easySummary": "A massive new study reveals that intelligence plays a surprisingly limited role in children&#039;s reading success, while visual processing showed no meaningful connection at all. Instead, the strongest predictors are sound recognition, vocabulary, and background knowledge, offering new clues about how to help struggling readers.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"Scientists identify two overlooked skills that predict reading success\"\n\nA massive new study reveals that intelligence plays a surprisingly limited role in children&#039;s reading success, while visual processing showed no meaningful connection at all. Instead, the strongest predictors are sound recognition, vocabulary, and background knowledge, offering new clues about how to help struggling readers.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
