costs in colder, energy-scarce states like Maine — an issue that some Democratic candidates are explicitly running on . “A system where you’re allowed to build the most economic energy resources with fewer encumbrances, fewer delays, and fewer restrictions is, almost by definition, a more affordable system,” Palken said. Thus, to green America’s grid — and save Americans’ money — Congress needs to cut red tape. They should waste little time in doing so.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
