      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhq-kuj2",
      "title": "Gabby Williams powers Valkyries past Dream in Game 7 for historic WNBA title",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Valkyries prevail 68-63 in league’s first-ever Game 7</p></li><li><p>Williams scores 30 as Golden State win first title</p></li><li><p>Second-year franchise complete remarkable rise</p></li></ul><p>In the middle of Chase Center, the Golden State Valkyries gathered somewhere they have been only a handful of times. They are, after all, just a second-year franchise.</p><p>But on Saturday night they came together to collect their trophy as WNBA champions. Kaila Charles embraced Tiffany Hayes as they jumped up and down. Kayla Thornton screamed towards the ceiling.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/31/golden-state-valkyries-atlanta-dream-wnba-finals-game-7-gabby-williams\">Continue reading...</a>",
