      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhr-w94u",
      "title": "‘Super proud’ De Minaur takes down new world No 1 Zverev to reach Vienna Open final",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>World No 10 holds nerve in 6-4, 1-6, 7-6 (7-4) semi-final win</p></li><li><p>Australian will meet Carlos Alcaraz in championship match</p></li></ul><p>Alex de Minaur has held his nerve to claim what could be one of the most significant wins of his career, downing the world No 1-elect Alexander Zverev with a fearless display of attacking tennis to reach the Vienna Open final.</p><p>The Australian played a fabulous deciding tiebreaker, nervelessly brushing off a couple of double faults to keep the pressure on the two-time grand slam champion to prevail 6-4, 1-6, 7-6 (7-4) to set up a championship match with Carlos Alcaraz at the Wiener Stadthalle.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/01/de-minaur-takes-down-zverev-to-reach-vienna-open-final-match-report-tennis\">Continue reading...</a>",
