      "title": "Breeders’ Cup 2026, day two: Moore’s ‘one bullet’ hits the target in Turf – as it happened",
      "description": "<p>Benvenuto Cellini and Ryan Moore quickened clear to win the $5m Breeders’ Cup Turf</p><p><strong>17.48 Breeders’ Cup Turf Sprint, Grade One, 5½f</strong></p><p>We’re on to the turf next, and the most obvious barrier to a European clean sweep on the grass in the form of Wesley Ward’s <strong>Bacio. </strong>He is already familiar to European racing fans as the winner of both the <strong>Palace of Holyroodhouse Handicap</strong> at Royal Ascot and the <strong>Nunthorpe</strong> at York in August.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2026/oct/31/breeders-cup-2026-day-two-live\">Continue reading...</a>",
