    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhm-412l",
      "title": "Lewis Hamilton storms to his first Ferrari pole at F1 Mexican GP with Antonelli fourth",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>George Russell second on grid after qualifying</p></li><li><p>Antonelli well placed as he nears title confirmation</p></li></ul><p>Even as Formula One’s young gun Kimi Antonelli remains on course to claim his first world championship on Sunday it was the veteran, seven-time champion Lewis Hamilton who gave a salutary reminder that there is very much fight left in the old dog yet as he claimed a spectacular pole position for the Mexico City Grand Prix.</p><p>Hamilton delivered a superb lap for Ferrari to secure his first pole for the team and just beat Mercedes’ George Russell into second. World champion <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/30/mexico-grand-prix-kimi-antonelli-f1-history\">in waiting Antonelli was in fourth place</a> but remains in position to close out the title on Sunday, although Hamilton and Russell, who must win the race to have any hope of keeping the fight alive, have at least locked out the front row.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/31/lewis-hamilton-storms-to-first-ferrari-pole-at-f1-mexican-grand-prix-with-antonelli-fifth\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/31/lewis-hamilton-storms-to-first-ferrari-pole-at-f1-mexican-grand-prix-with-antonelli-fifth",
