        "Categorized under Sports for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by The Guardian Sport. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "<ul><li><p>Bayern Munich held to 2-2 draw after Silva equaliser</p></li><li><p>Barcelona on top of La Liga after thrashng Alaves </p></li></ul><p>The Ballon d’Or winner Harry Kane missed a penalty and hit the post for ⁠<strong>Bayern Munich</strong> as <strong>Borussia Dortmund</strong> snatched a last-gasp equaliser through Fabio Silva for a 2-2 draw ⁠in Der Klassiker on ⁠Saturday ​that kept the teams level on points at the top.</p><p>Kane, who collected his prize in a ceremony ⁠in London on Monday, was an unused substitute in the 6-1 German Cup second-round demolition of Magdeburg on Wednesday ⁠but returned to the starting lineup on Saturday, missing from the spot with Bayern 1-0 up. He also hit ​the post, one of four ‌times Bayern struck ‌the woodwork. Silva snatched the equaliser in the 89th minute to leave both ‌teams on 18 points, with Bayern top on goal difference.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/european-football-harry-kane-bayern-munich-borussia-dortmund-milan-inter-barcelona\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian Sport, this report highlights developments in Sports.\n\nHeadline: \"European football: Kane misses penalty as Dortmund share spoils in Der Klassiker\"\n\n<ul><li><p>Bayern Munich held to 2-2 draw after Silva equaliser</p></li><li><p>Barcelona on top of La Liga after thrashng Alaves </p></li></ul><p>The Ballon d’Or winner Harry Kane missed a penalty and hit the post for ⁠<strong>Bayern Munich</strong> as <strong>Borussia Dortmund</strong> snatched a last-gasp equaliser through Fabio Silva for a 2-2 draw ⁠in Der Klassiker on ⁠Saturday ​that kept the teams level on points at the top.</p><p>Kane, who collected his prize in a ceremony ⁠in London on Monday, was an unused substitute in the 6-1 German Cup second-round demolition of Magdeburg on Wednesday ⁠but returned to the starting lineup on Saturday, missing from the spot with Bayern 1-0 up. He also hit ​the post, one of four ‌times Bayern struck ‌the woodwork. Silva snatched the equaliser in the 89th minute to leave both ‌teams on 18 points, with Bayern top on goal difference.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/european-football-harry-kane-bayern-munich-borussia-dortmund-milan-inter-barcelona\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
