    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhu-3zwc",
      "title": "Naderi breaks Aberdeen’s resistance as Rangers reach Premier Sports Cup final",
      "description": "<p>Ryan Naderi’s dramatic late strike broke down Aberdeen’s stubborn resistance to earn Rangers a place in the Premier Sports Cup final.</p><p>Aberdeen restricted Rangers to one shot on target in a low quality first half, but Derek McInnes’s side picked up the pace after the break. Aberdeen survived relentless pressure at times but in the 83rd minute Naderi redirected a strike from James Penrice into the net for his eighth goal of the season to seal a 1-0 win at Hampden Park.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/rangers-aberdeen-scottish-league-cup-semi-final-match-report\">Continue reading...</a>",
