    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhn-6ftl",
      "title": "Enzo Maresca rues ‘silly’ errors after Manchester City defeat against Brighton",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Matheus Nunes mistake lets in Yasin Ayari for winner</p></li><li><p>Maresca: ‘We are conceding silly goals that we can avoid’</p></li></ul><p>Enzo Maresca said “silly goals” and individual errors are costing Manchester City after Matheus Nunes’ mistake allowed Yasin Ayari to score <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/manchester-city-brighton-premier-league-match-report\">Brighton’s winner in Saturday’s 1-0 victory</a> here. Ayari’s strike was made possible after Nunes, City’s right-back, missed Diego Gómez’s cross from the right, so the ball could come back across goal via Maxim De Cuyper.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/24/aston-villa-manchester-city-premier-league-match-report\">2-1 loss at Aston Villa</a> came from Gianluigi Donnarumma allowing Nicolas Jackson’s long-range winner to squeeze under his body.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/enzo-maresca-manchester-city-brighton-premier-league\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/enzo-maresca-manchester-city-brighton-premier-league",
