      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pch-kbpr",
      "title": "Protests under way in Germany and France as minister warns against use of Halloween masks – as it happened",
      "description": "<p>France’s interior minister, Laurent Nuñez, has warned protesters that covering their faces with Halloween costumes could result in fines</p><ul><li><p>Full report: <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/31/police-clash-rioters-after-largely-peaceful-protests-across-france\">Police clash with masked rioters after largely peaceful protests across France</a></p></li></ul><p>Protesters in <strong>Paris</strong> have begun marching from Porte de Bagnolet, with demonstrations also taking place in <strong>Lille</strong> and <strong>Lyon</strong>.</p><p>Crowds of people have gathered in Paris for the protests, where two French student unions <strong>have called for a blockade of schools and universities</strong> on Tuesday and Thursday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/31/france-germany-protests-paris-europe-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
