    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pcl-rt8t",
      "title": "Almost 140 arrested at protest against Palestine Action ban outside US embassy in London",
      "description": "<p>Met alleges demonstrators ‘meeting to purposefully commit a crime’ in largest such gathering under Burnham</p><p>Almost 140 people have been arrested at the largest mass demonstrations under Andy Burnham’s premiership opposing the proscription of Palestine Action.</p><p>Hundreds of people gathered outside the US embassy in Battersea, south London, holding signs that read: “I oppose genocide, I support Palestine Action.” Demonstrators also held a vigil in support of the group outside the US consulate in Edinburgh.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/31/protest-against-palestine-action-ban-outside-us-embassy-in-london\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/31/protest-against-palestine-action-ban-outside-us-embassy-in-london",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/31/protest-against-palestine-action-ban-outside-us-embassy-in-london",
      "publisherId": "guardian_world",
