    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhs-l2di",
      "title": "Packers’ Josh Jacobs faces fresh abuse allegations from three women in police records",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Three women contacted police after Jacobs’ May arrest</p></li><li><p>One alleged the Packers star threatened to kill her</p></li><li><p>Lawyers call allegations ‘uncorroborated’ and ‘old’</p></li></ul><p>As police investigated the battery case involving Green Bay Packers running back Josh Jacobs following a May altercation with his then-girlfriend, multiple other women contacted them to detail their own allegations against him.</p><p>Those accounts were included in evidence regarding Jacobs’ battery case that the Hobart/Lawrence Police Department released on Friday night in response to a public records request. Green Bay TV station NBC 26 first reported the records’ release.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/31/josh-jacobs-green-bay-packers-abuse-allegations-police-records\">Continue reading...</a>",
