    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhv-9pou",
      "title": "‘I’m not here to be liked’: Glasner defiant as Brentford capitalise on Forest woes",
      "description": "<p>For Oliver Glasner and Nottingham Forest, the future starts now. His post-match press conference lasted 14 frustrated minutes in which, repeatedly banging the desk, he blamed himself for compromising his principles and told players that if they didn’t “buy in” they could “leave”.</p><p>“For me, I go home and have breakfast with my family, so it’s not the worst situation,” Glasner said. “Nobody needs to have pity with Oliver Glasner. If I want, I could start in two weeks somewhere else. I won’t do it. But the players, the staff, they remain in the same situation. And it’s the same shit situation that the club had last year. So you need to change and rebuild from the bottom to the top. And this is clear for me. And this is what I will do. And without any compromises, zero, zero.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/brentford-nottingham-forest-premier-league-match-report\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/brentford-nottingham-forest-premier-league-match-report",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/brentford-nottingham-forest-premier-league-match-report",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Sport",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardiansport",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Sports",
      "currentAffairsCategory": "Sports",
      "publishDate": "2026-10-31T17:09:34.000Z",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-31T17:09:34.000Z",
      "firstSeenAt": "2026-11-01T04:59:15.864Z",
      "lastCheckedAt": "2026-11-01T05:06:57.163Z",
      "contentHash": "c756b0a50fbec196",
      "isUpdate": false,
      "readingTimeMinutes": 5,
