    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pcn-lwe2",
      "title": "More than 50m Americans cast ballots in early voting with three days to go before midterms",
      "description": "<p>Record number of early votes cast, with Democrats outnumbering Republicans in states which collect that information</p><p>There has been a surge of early voting for the US midterm elections, with millions more Americans going to the polls compared with the last such election amid a series of tight contests that will determine control of Congress.</p><p>More than 50.5m early votes have been cast across the US as of Saturday morning, <a href=\"https://election.lab.ufl.edu/early-vote/2026-early-voting/\">according to an analysis by the University of Florida</a>. This is already nearly 5m more votes than the total number of early votes made in the last midterm elections, in 2022.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/31/early-voting-midterms\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/31/early-voting-midterms",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/31/early-voting-midterms",
      "publisherId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian World",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardianworld",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585829365295-ab7cd400c167?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Current Affairs",
      "currentAffairsCategory": "World News",
      "publishDate": "2026-10-31T16:13:17.000Z",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-31T16:13:17.000Z",
      "firstSeenAt": "2026-11-01T04:59:20.856Z",
      "lastCheckedAt": "2026-11-01T05:04:10.395Z",
