    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pcm-xs25",
      "title": "A world-first focus on long-term outcomes could transform UK government – or create new spending fights",
      "description": "<p>Tucked away in John Healey’s budget is decision to ringfence preventative projects where future savings outweigh initial cost</p><p>It merited the briefest of mentions in John Healey’s speech and just one paragraph in the 166-page <a href=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ae20b85460c1346f7be784e/E03668986_HMT_Budget_2026_ELAY__2_.pdf\">budget document</a>, but some believe it could revolutionise not just public spending but the very process of government itself: a new focus on long-term outcomes.</p><p>The idea in the broad sense is very simple. Any spending deemed to be “preventative” – that is, the initial outlay will be more than made up for by future savings – will from now on be ringfenced, meaning it cannot be raided for more immediate needs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/31/spending-plan-long-term-focus-uk-government\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/31/spending-plan-long-term-focus-uk-government",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/31/spending-plan-long-term-focus-uk-government",
      "publisherId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian World",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardianworld",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585829365295-ab7cd400c167?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
