    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pcn-m0zv",
      "title": "Ads accusing Republican candidates of protecting Epstein fill airwaves in final midterm push",
      "description": "<p>But select Democrats, too, are being accused of having ties to the late sex offender as country prepares to vote</p><p>In races across the country, Democratic candidates or groups that support them have released ads accusing <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans\">Republicans</a> of protecting pedophiles by voting against legislation to release files related to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein\">Jeffrey Epstein</a>.</p><p>The ads appear intended to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/22/trump-epstein-tucker-carlson-turning-point-usa\">evoke an emotional response </a>by accusing candidates of “protecting” Epstein, a notorious pedophile accused of running a sex-trafficking ring involving minors.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/31/political-ads-midterms-epstein-republican-candidate\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/31/political-ads-midterms-epstein-republican-candidate",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/31/political-ads-midterms-epstein-republican-candidate",
      "publisherId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian World",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardianworld",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585829365295-ab7cd400c167?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
