      "title": "‘We need to be better’: Manchester United’s Olid demands progress after Everton draw",
      "description": "<p>A group of well-choreographed, fancy-dress-wearing school-age dancers fully embraced the Halloween spirit on Saturday as they boogied to one of Michael Jackson’s greatest hits at half-time here. Alas, the match itself was no thriller.</p><p>For Manchester United, the only scary thing about this game was how little they tested Courtney Brosnan in Everton’s goal in the first 75 minutes as they demonstrated their lack of creativity.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/31/everton-manchester-united-wsl-match-report\">Continue reading...</a>",
