      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pcm-xooq",
      "title": "UK police should not have let US force take over airbase trial, MoD documents show",
      "description": "<p>According to documents obtained by the Guardian, officials accused Cambridgeshire force of breaching US-UK deal by handing over case of woman strangled by US pilot</p><p>Ministry of Defence officials have privately accused a UK police force of wrongly handing over the investigation of an American fighter pilot who strangled a British woman to the US military, according to documents obtained by the Guardian.</p><p>Cambridgeshire police allowed the US military police to quickly take control of the investigation into Capt Jacob Wulfson after he had been accused of sexually<strong> </strong>assaulting Sarah Steele in his Cambridge flat.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/31/uk-police-should-not-have-let-us-force-take-over-airbase-trial-mod-documents-show\">Continue reading...</a>",
