        "Original reporting published by The Guardian World. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "<p>Rex Patrick’s latest transparency fight is over what he calls ‘most open secret in the history of Australian spying’ – maybe even the world</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A campaign to uncover any documents relating to whether <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2019/aug/10/witness-k-and-the-outrageous-spy-scandal-that-failed-to-shame-australia\">Australian spies bugged Timor-Leste</a> to gain the upper hand in sensitive oil and gas negotiations will be a little less secret after a critical win by the former senator Rex Patrick.</p><p>The politician turned transparency advocate is trying to finally lift the lid on the top-secret mission in 2004 that became a public scandal years later after an ex-spy and a former attorney general <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2015/may/04/east-timor-welcomes-australias-return-of-spying-documents-seized-by-asio\">attempted to mount a case in The Hague</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/timor-leste-australia-bugging-rex-patrick-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian World, this report highlights developments in World News.\n\nHeadline: \"A top-secret spy mission, a decades-old scandal – and the Austin Powers-esque saga to lift the lid\"\n\n<p>Rex Patrick’s latest transparency fight is over what he calls ‘most open secret in the history of Australian spying’ – maybe even the world</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A campaign to uncover any documents relating to whether <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2019/aug/10/witness-k-and-the-outrageous-spy-scandal-that-failed-to-shame-australia\">Australian spies bugged Timor-Leste</a> to gain the upper hand in sensitive oil and gas negotiations will be a little less secret after a critical win by the former senator Rex Patrick.</p><p>The politician turned transparency advocate is trying to finally lift the lid on the top-secret mission in 2004 that became a public scandal years later after an ex-spy and a former attorney general <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2015/may/04/east-timor-welcomes-australias-return-of-spying-documents-seized-by-asio\">attempted to mount a case in The Hague</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/timor-leste-australia-bugging-rex-patrick-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
