    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhp-ftua",
      "title": "Arteta can take inspiration from George Graham to expunge painful Anfield memories",
      "description": "<p>Arsenal have not won at Liverpool for 13 league games but Gunners’ win in 1989 remains one of club’s greatest nights</p><p>Mikel Arteta used a Spanish word to describe what it felt like to be helpless at Anfield while playing for Everton in 2011: <em>bajar</em>. “It’s when a cyclist is going up and looks amazing, then in one kilometre he goes ‘boom’ and he’s struggling again,” he said in Amazon’s All or Nothing documentary. “The game was going well and then suddenly I could only see red shirts flying around. The game is passing all over me and I cannot react. I only had that feeling in my career once, and it was at Anfield.”</p><p>Given Arteta’s record at Liverpool, Sunday’s showdown with his childhood friend Andoni Iraola – five days after Arsenal were <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/27/fleetwood-town-arsenal-carabao-cup-fourth-round-match-report\">dumped out of the Carabao Cup by Fleetwood</a> – could be expected to fill him with dread. Arteta finally tasted victory there as a player with Arsenal <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2012/sep/02/liverpool-arsenal-premier-league-match-report\">in September 2012</a>, after five failed attempts in the Merseyside derby, but ended up spending the night in hospital with concussion after colliding with Jordan Henderson in an incident he has described as “the biggest fear of my life”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/30/mikel-arteta-arsenal-inspiration-george-graham-anfield-liverpool\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/30/mikel-arteta-arsenal-inspiration-george-graham-anfield-liverpool",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/30/mikel-arteta-arsenal-inspiration-george-graham-anfield-liverpool",
