    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhs-a6f8",
      "title": "Fiesta awaits in Mexico City as Kimi Antonelli speeds towards F1 history",
      "description": "<p>Italian 20-year-old is on the verge of becoming the youngest world champion with the Mexican Grand Prix ready for a carnival coronation atmosphere</p><p>An undeniable highlight of this Formula One season, marked by discontent at the new regulations, has been getting swept along by the sheer joy that the world champion-in-waiting, Kimi Antonelli, has displayed on his way to a title he will almost surely secure this weekend at the Mexican Grand Prix.</p><p>Antonelli was still a teenager for the first half of the year and it seemed fitting to describe him as such. His exuberant embrace of competing for Mercedes <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/23/kimi-antonelli-f1-champion-elect\">at the sharp end of F1</a> in just his second season was that of any 19-year-old. Like discovering a life-changing new band or how much fun can be had with a cold beer, a wide grin was barely off his face.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/30/mexico-grand-prix-kimi-antonelli-f1-history\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/30/mexico-grand-prix-kimi-antonelli-f1-history",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/30/mexico-grand-prix-kimi-antonelli-f1-history",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
