    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pcd-72ew",
      "title": "‘Amateur morons’: Flávio Bolsonaro’s short-lived ‘president-elect’ claim met with mockery",
      "description": "<p>Brazilian media ridicule defeated candidate over ‘shameful’ absconsion to US and bizarre letter with wrong coat of arms</p><p>Flávio Bolsonaro had hoped that by Sunday night people would be calling him the next president of Brazil.</p><p>Instead, the far-right politician’s decision to flee to the US after losing the election and – for 58 minutes – to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/flavio-bolsonaro-miami-us-fleeing-brazilian-election-defeat\">declare himself “Brazil’s true president-elect”</a>, has made him a laughing stock, with Brazilian newspapers and commentators raining a barrage of scornful adjectives down on the conquered candidate.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/flavio-bolsonaros-president-elect-claim-mockery-brazil\">Continue reading...</a>",
