      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mvxd1pha-5wvo",
      "title": "Freakish frocks and ghoulish guises: last-minute Halloween costumes that won’t haunt the environment",
      "description": "<p>Keen to join in the revelry but don’t have a costume? You can still fashion a get-up without buying – or wasting – anything</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/change-by-degrees\">Change by degrees</a> offers life hacks and sustainable living tips each Saturday to help reduce your household’s carbon footprint</p></li><li><p>Got a question or tip for reducing household emissions? Email us at <a href=\"mailto:changebydegrees@theguardian.com\">changebydegrees@theguardian.com</a></p></li></ul><p>The thrill of an event like Halloween doesn’t come from a brand new costume or “two pillowcases’ worth of sweets”, says play specialist Cat Sewell.</p><p>The fun comes from carving out the time to play, making ridiculous outfits, and the terror and delight of haunting the neighbourhood, says the artistic director and co-CEO of Polyglot Theatre, a company that creates participatory, immersive, child-led theatre.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/last-minute-halloween-costumes-that-wont-haunt-the-environment\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/last-minute-halloween-costumes-that-wont-haunt-the-environment",
