      "easySummary": "<p>In today’s newsletter: Benjamin Netanyahu has been left without a majority, now it is up to the coalition to find out whether the desire for change will prove to be a defining political moment</p><p>Good morning. It was described by many Israelis as the most consequential election in their country’s history. And, as the final votes were tallied, it has delivered a result that presents Israel with a significant dilemma.</p><p>Benjamin Netanyahu’s far-right coalition has lost its mandate while the opposition has a clear majority: but only if the Jewish Israeli opposition bloc, led by retired general Gadi Eisenkot, is prepared to make a governing pact with Palestinian Israeli parties, which have secured a historic result.</p><p><em><strong>UK politics </strong></em>| John Healey <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/29/john-healey-budget-backs-away-from-cutting-welfare-public-finance-shortfall\">has backed away</a> from cutting the cost of welfare this parliament, amid dire warnings his first budget could lead to brutal spending cuts because of a £28bn shortfall in public finances.</p><p><em><strong>Patrick Stewart </strong></em>| The acclaimed British stage and screen actor renowned for both Shakespeare and sci-fi,<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/oct/29/patrick-stewart-dead\"> died at his home </a>in Los Angeles after “a brief and poignant journey with Alzheimer’s disease and Lewy body dementia”, his longtime spokesperson said.</p><p><em><strong>Environment </strong></em>| One of the most <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/30/wildlife-trusts-northumberland-nature-recovery-rothbury-estate\">ambitious nature recovery projects</a> ever undertaken in England can go ahead after campaigners announced they had raised £30m to buy an estate in Northumberland.</p><p><em><strong>Europe </strong></em>| Spain began three days of mourning on Thursday for at least 69 people <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/29/spain-mourning-period-deadly-train-crash\">who died in a high-speed rail collision</a>, as hospitals continued to treat dozens of injured passengers and train drivers went on strike to urge more investment in railway safety.</p><p><em><strong>US news </strong></em>| The Trump administration <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/29/trump-administration-california-noncitizen-voting-investigation\">has opened a criminal investigation </a>in California over claims that thousands of noncitizens are registered to vote in the state, and has begun subpoenaing election officials.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/friday-briefing-israel-has-a-dilemma-can-its-opposition-govern-with-palestinian-parties\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian World, this report highlights developments in World News.\n\nHeadline: \"Friday briefing: Israel has a dilemma - can its opposition govern with Palestinian parties?\"\n\n<p>In today’s newsletter: Benjamin Netanyahu has been left without a majority, now it is up to the coalition to find out whether the desire for change will prove to be a defining political moment</p><p>Good morning. It was described by many Israelis as the most consequential election in their country’s history. And, as the final votes were tallied, it has delivered a result that presents Israel with a significant dilemma.</p><p>Benjamin Netanyahu’s far-right coalition has lost its mandate while the opposition has a clear majority: but only if the Jewish Israeli opposition bloc, led by retired general Gadi Eisenkot, is prepared to make a governing pact with Palestinian Israeli parties, which have secured a historic result.</p><p><em><strong>UK politics </strong></em>| John Healey <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/29/john-healey-budget-backs-away-from-cutting-welfare-public-finance-shortfall\">has backed away</a> from cutting the cost of welfare this parliament, amid dire warnings his first budget could lead to brutal spending cuts because of a £28bn shortfall in public finances.</p><p><em><strong>Patrick Stewart </strong></em>| The acclaimed British stage and screen actor renowned for both Shakespeare and sci-fi,<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/oct/29/patrick-stewart-dead\"> died at his home </a>in Los Angeles after “a brief and poignant journey with Alzheimer’s disease and Lewy body dementia”, his longtime spokesperson said.</p><p><em><strong>Environment </strong></em>| One of the most <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/30/wildlife-trusts-northumberland-nature-recovery-rothbury-estate\">ambitious nature recovery projects</a> ever undertaken in England can go ahead after campaigners announced they had raised £30m to buy an estate in Northumberland.</p><p><em><strong>Europe </strong></em>| Spain began three days of mourning on Thursday for at least 69 people <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/29/spain-mourning-period-deadly-train-crash\">who died in a high-speed rail collision</a>, as hospitals continued to treat dozens of injured passengers and train drivers went on strike to urge more investment in railway safety.</p><p><em><strong>US news </strong></em>| The Trump administration <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/29/trump-administration-california-noncitizen-voting-investigation\">has opened a criminal investigation </a>in California over claims that thousands of noncitizens are registered to vote in the state, and has begun subpoenaing election officials.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/friday-briefing-israel-has-a-dilemma-can-its-opposition-govern-with-palestinian-parties\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
