      "title": "Legal loopholes and weak enforcement leave India&#8217;s exotic pet trade hard to police",
      "description": "Rising disposable incomes, social media algorithms, and pop culture influences have led to a surge in demand for exotic pets in India, reports Mongabay India’s Arathi Menon. A recent report by the Humane World for Animals (HWA) valued India’s exotic pet market at $42.6 million in 2024, and projected it will nearly double by 2030. [&#8230;]",
