      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvxd1pcf-ad27",
      "title": "El Niño-driven drought in Papua New Guinea a ‘national crisis’ as rivers dry up and local farms fail",
      "description": "<p>As many as 8 million people have been affected by food shortages, electricity blackouts and health clinic closures</p><p>Extreme drought driven by an historic El Niño is affecting as many as 8 million people in Papua New Guinea, causing a cascade of issues from shortages of food and water, to electricity scarcity and schooling disruption.</p><p>An influential coalition that includes churches, trade unions and business groups has said the Pacific nation is in the midst of a “national crisis”, but there appears to be “no coordinated plan to protect vulnerable communities from the worsening impacts of El Niño.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/png-el-nino-drought-papua-new-guinea\">Continue reading...</a>",
