      "id": "art-mongabay-mvxd1nfz-m5x0",
      "title": "In Suriname’s Amazon, the Wayana community struggling to keep gold miners at bay",
      "description": "KAWEMHAKAN, Suriname — Beneath thousands of square kilometers of rainforest here lie vast deposits of gold and other minerals. Around a million ounces are extracted legally every year, but much more remains buried throughout the Amazon. In some of the farthest-flung parts of the rainforest, such as these small villages along the border with French [&#8230;]",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://news.mongabay.com/2026/10/in-surinames-amazon-the-wayana-community-struggling-to-keep-gold-miners-at-bay",
