      "title": "Einstein&#039;s equations may explain the universe without dark energy",
      "description": "Mathematicians have uncovered what they argue is a fundamental flaw in the standard model of the universe, potentially challenging the need for dark energy. Their calculations suggest that the mathematical framework used to describe cosmic expansion is inherently unstable and that the universe could accelerate naturally under Einstein&#039;s original theory of gravity. The findings also raise surprising questions about whether our location in the universe is as ordinary as scientists have long assumed.",
