      "easySummary": "Researchers have discovered a surprising hidden ability in Europe&#039;s familiar black-and-yellow fire salamanders: they glow green and cyan under ultraviolet light. The mysterious fluorescence comes mainly from glands in their skin and their toxic secretions, which can continue glowing for more than 24 hours after being released.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"Scientists discover a secret glow in toxic fire salamanders\"\n\nResearchers have discovered a surprising hidden ability in Europe&#039;s familiar black-and-yellow fire salamanders: they glow green and cyan under ultraviolet light. The mysterious fluorescence comes mainly from glands in their skin and their toxic secretions, which can continue glowing for more than 24 hours after being released.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
