      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mvxd1phb-wj87",
      "title": "Will it be AI or the climate crisis that ends humanity? We can make it neither | Adam McKay and Philip Eubanks",
      "description": "<p>Both of these threats have the same roots: private entities seeking to cash in. We have the power to stand against them</p><p>A summer of extreme heat, entire villages obliterated in Nepal, a super <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/elnino\">El Niño</a> breaking records, Exxon <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/exxon-raises-2050-global-emissions-forecast-sees-slower-coal-decline-2026-09-17/\">publicly saying</a> we may reach 3C by 2050 – could it possibly be any worse?</p><p>How about throwing <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai\">AI</a> extinction in the mix?</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/oct/28/ai-climate-crisis-humanity\">Continue reading...</a>",
