      "easySummary": "<p>Jean Kaseya, of the Africa CDC, warns of the illness spreading like Covid unless more funding is secured to increase preparedness and possible treatment</p><p>The “unprecedented” <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/17/what-is-ebola-why-who-says-drc-uganda-outbreak-global-health-emergency\">spread of the Ebola outbreak</a> means it could reach the UK and other countries, according to one of Africa’s top health officials.</p><p>As the current outbreak reached <a href=\"https://www.ecdc.europa.eu/en/ebola-disease-multi-country-outbreak-2026\">10,000 cases, with almost 5,000 deaths</a>, Dr Jean Kaseya, director general of the Africa Centres for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), compared the outbreak to the Covid pandemic, which first took hold in China before spreading to countries across the world, claiming millions of lives, and ravaging health systems and economies.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/28/africa-ebola-outbreak-could-reach-uk-says-top-health-official\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian World, this report highlights developments in World News.\n\nHeadline: \"Africa’s ‘unprecedented’ Ebola outbreak could reach UK, says top health official\"\n\n<p>Jean Kaseya, of the Africa CDC, warns of the illness spreading like Covid unless more funding is secured to increase preparedness and possible treatment</p><p>The “unprecedented” <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/17/what-is-ebola-why-who-says-drc-uganda-outbreak-global-health-emergency\">spread of the Ebola outbreak</a> means it could reach the UK and other countries, according to one of Africa’s top health officials.</p><p>As the current outbreak reached <a href=\"https://www.ecdc.europa.eu/en/ebola-disease-multi-country-outbreak-2026\">10,000 cases, with almost 5,000 deaths</a>, Dr Jean Kaseya, director general of the Africa Centres for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), compared the outbreak to the Covid pandemic, which first took hold in China before spreading to countries across the world, claiming millions of lives, and ravaging health systems and economies.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/28/africa-ebola-outbreak-could-reach-uk-says-top-health-official\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
