    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1lhx-6v67",
      "title": "Jimmy Anderson’s stubborn refusal to give up has fuelled his greatest achievements | Emma John",
      "description": "<p>Lancashire have moved on without him, but the 44-year-old England stalwart wants to keep going as long as his body allows</p><p>Jimmy Anderson could teach Philip Marlowe a thing or two about The Long Goodbye. England’s leading wicket-taker in Tests is of that sporting breed who have no interest in bowing out at the top. <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2019/dec/25/andy-murray-melbourne--finish-australian-open\">Like Andy Murray before him</a>, he has shown little enthusiasm to bow out at all, as long as his body allows him to keep doing the thing he loves: getting opposition batsmen out.</p><p>It was little surprise, then, that when Lancashire announced this week they <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/jimmy-anderson-set-to-retire-from-cricket-lancashire-contract\">would not be renewing his contract</a> after 25 years, there was no immediate retirement announcement. Instead there was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/25/jimmy-anderson-confirms-lancashire-exit-cricket\">an irked Instagram post</a>, then silence, as the one-club man considered his options. One of those, apparently, was a T10 cricket tournament in Rome. And lo, it is now confirmed that Anderson will lead (and even “co-own”) the Napoli Knights for 12 days next month.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/28/cricket-jimmy-anderson-england-lancashire-stubborn-farewell-tour\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/28/cricket-jimmy-anderson-england-lancashire-stubborn-farewell-tour",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/28/cricket-jimmy-anderson-england-lancashire-stubborn-farewell-tour",
