    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvxd1li0-ydaw",
      "title": "Which footballers have scored in the same minute as their surname? | The Knowledge",
      "description": "<p>Plus: the longest home droughts, pre-Christmas goal centuries and the first official club websites</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"mailto:knowledge@theguardian.com\"><strong>Mail us</strong></a><strong> with all of your questions and answers</strong></p></li></ul><p><strong>“Justin Seven-Seven came on in the 75th minute and then scored in the 77th minute for West Brom Under-21s against Sutton United in the National League Cup. You have probably already guessed my question, but has anyone else ever scored in the same minute as their name?”</strong> wonders Peter Skilton.</p><p>Readers of a certain age may recall <strong>Didier Six</strong>, the mercurial French winger who had a brief spell at Aston Villa in 1984-85. A number of you mentioned some or all of the following sixth-minute goals, which includes two in consecutive seasons against Bordeaux:</p><p><strong>Valenciennes 2-1 Nancy (agg: 2-3)</strong> Coupe de France quarter-final, 1975-76</p><p><strong>Valenciennes 3-2 Bordeaux</strong> Ligue 1, 1976-77</p><p><strong>Lens 2-0 Bordeaux</strong> Ligue 1, 1977-78</p><p><strong>VfB Stuttgart 5-1 Karlsruher</strong> Bundesliga, 1981-82</p><p><strong>Bundesliga</strong> 71 goals in 18 games</p><p><strong>Champions League</strong> 18 goals in 6 games</p><p><strong>DFB-Pokal</strong> 10 goals in 3 games</p><p><strong>Franz Beckenbauer Supercup</strong> 2 goals in 1 game</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/28/which-footballers-have-scored-in-the-same-minute-as-their-surname-knowledge\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/28/which-footballers-have-scored-in-the-same-minute-as-their-surname-knowledge",
