      "quickSummary": [
        "Official verified dispatch from ScienceDaily: \"James Webb discovers a scorching lava planet with a “giant sunscreen”\".",
        "Key Context: A scorching lava planet 280 light-years away has surprised astronomers by apparently maintaining a thick atmosphere despite conditions that should have stripped it away billions of years ago. James We.",
        "Categorized under Health for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by ScienceDaily. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "A scorching lava planet 280 light-years away has surprised astronomers by apparently maintaining a thick atmosphere despite conditions that should have stripped it away billions of years ago. James Webb Space Telescope observations suggest that TOI-561 b reflects about 75% of incoming starlight, possibly because of mineral clouds that act like a giant sunscreen. The planet may also be continually replenishing its atmosphere through gases released from a global ocean of molten rock.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"James Webb discovers a scorching lava planet with a “giant sunscreen”\"\n\nA scorching lava planet 280 light-years away has surprised astronomers by apparently maintaining a thick atmosphere despite conditions that should have stripped it away billions of years ago. James Webb Space Telescope observations suggest that TOI-561 b reflects about 75% of incoming starlight, possibly because of mineral clouds that act like a giant sunscreen. The planet may also be continually replenishing its atmosphere through gases released from a global ocean of molten rock.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
