    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvpeg0pj-ns8n",
      "title": "Brazil runoff live updates: world leaders congratulate Lula on historic election win as Bolsonaro refuses to concede",
      "description": "<p>Leftist president Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva defeated the far-right senator and was elected president of Brazil for a fourth non-consecutive term</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/lula-wins-brazil-election\">Full report: Lula wins fourth term as Brazil’s president over Flávio Bolsonaro</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-2026-live-second-round-results\">Live second round results</a></p></li></ul><p>The local electoral court ordered the immediate restoration of 100% of the bus fleet and ordered the arrest of the municipal transport secretary, Pablo Souza, on suspicion of an electoral offence and disobeying court orders. The arrest warrant could not be carried out, however, because he is in Paris on what the city government described as an “official mission”, and is not expected to return to Brazil until Monday.</p><p>Late in the afternoon, Flávio Bolsonaro also filed requests for voting to be extended by two hours in cities in the states of São Paulo, Paraná and Santa Catarina, but because of heavy rain that he said had prevented voters from turning out.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula",
      "publisherId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian World",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardianworld",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585829365295-ab7cd400c167?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Current Affairs",
      "currentAffairsCategory": "World News",
      "publishDate": "2026-10-26T14:58:23.000Z",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T14:58:23.000Z",
      "firstSeenAt": "2026-10-26T15:16:18.977Z",
      "lastCheckedAt": "2026-10-26T15:23:12.047Z",
      "contentHash": "13a136cd3d509391",
      "isUpdate": false,
      "readingTimeMinutes": 5,
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/12419465c89789c79295caff90cc2957feb4543c/512_0_3320_2656/master/3320.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=7337aafc4dbcda473a7689df2cacc5f2&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "originalImageUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/12419465c89789c79295caff90cc2957feb4543c/512_0_3320_2656/master/3320.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=7337aafc4dbcda473a7689df2cacc5f2&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "imageSource": "publisher",
