    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvpeg0pn-bpu8",
      "title": "Serbia wakes up to new reality after student-led movement ousts Vučić – Europe live",
      "description": "<p>Hopes raised for a reset in relations with EU and other partners following the defeat of authoritarian president</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/25/serbian-leader-aleksandar-vucic-concedes-defeat-in-fiercely-contested-parliamentary-election\">Serbian leader ousted by student movement in seismic election</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Back to Serbia, we are expecting to hear from two groups of election monitors in the coming hours:</strong> first, <em>very</em> shortly, from Serbia’s Center for Research, Transparency and Accountability (CRTA), and then a bit later from a group of international observers, including from the OSCE, the ODIHR, and the European parliament.</p><p>I will keep an eye on their findings and bring you the key lines.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/26/serbia-vucic-elections-students-bulgaria-france-urkaine-russia-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/26/serbia-vucic-elections-students-bulgaria-france-urkaine-russia-latest-news-updates",
