      "title": "Audi boss under fire in Germany for Trump rally appearance",
      "description": "<p>Gernot Döllner criticised for in-person announcement of major investment in US days before midterm elections</p><p>The head of the luxury carmaker Audi is under fire in Germany for appearing at a rally with <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a> just days before the US midterm elections, to announce billions of dollars of investment in battleground state Georgia.</p><p>Gernot Döllner joined Trump on stage after the US president gave a speech criticised by the head of an elected body of employees at Audi’s parent company, Volkswagen, as being full of “racism, sexism, transphobia [and] contempt for democracy”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/audi-boss-under-fire-in-germany-for-trump-rally-appearance\">Continue reading...</a>",
