    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvpeg0pr-zvyq",
      "title": "Unions suspend planned V&A strike after improved pay offer",
      "description": "<p>London sites to remain open as Prospect and PCS agree to ‘Acas-facilitated talks’ with museum management</p><p>A planned strike at the V&amp;A over half-term has been suspended after an improved offer from its management.</p><p>Museum staff who were members of the Prospect and Public and Commercial Services (PCS) unions had voted to strike on Thursday and Friday in a dispute over pay and working conditions including <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2026/jul/29/v-and-a-museum-storehouse-london-vote-strike\">inadequate toilet and hydration breaks</a>. The strike would have <a href=\"https://archive.ph/ckBX0\">closed</a> the V&amp;A’s main galleries in south Kensington, as well as V&amp;A East, V&amp;A Storehouse and Young V&amp;A in east London.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2026/oct/26/v-and-a-museum-unions-suspend-strike-after-improved-pay-offer-london\">Continue reading...</a>",
