    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvpccgs2-vi1p",
      "title": "TNT Sports close to securing live UK rights for England white-ball cricket tour of Australia",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Channel 5 in advanced talks over highlights package</p></li><li><p>Opening game may be also be free-to-air in deal</p></li></ul><p>TNT Sports is close to securing live UK rights for England’s white-ball tour of Australia next month in a deal that could see one of the matches broadcast free-to-air (FTA) on Channel 5.</p><p>The Guardian has learned that Channel 5 is also in advanced talks with Cricket Australia over a highlights package for the eight-match tour, with the terrestrial broadcaster also in discussions over securing live rights for one of the five T20 internationals.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/26/tnt-sports-close-to-securing-live-uk-rights-england-white-ball-limited-overs-tour-australia-cricket\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/26/tnt-sports-close-to-securing-live-uk-rights-england-white-ball-limited-overs-tour-australia-cricket",
