      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mvpeg0uo-ngu0",
      "title": "Sunlight at night: US startup’s demonstration of lighting Earth from space draws critcism",
      "description": "<p>Company imitates reflection of sun from mirrors, prompting pushback from some scientists, environmentalists and California locals</p><p>Locals in a rural area of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california\">California</a> were recently startled to see dazzlingly bright light shining down from nearby mountains at night, illuminating a swathe of the desert below.</p><p>Unbeknown to them, the strange nocturnal illumination was the latest step in a company’s plan to erect thousands of giant mirrors in space to reflect sunlight on to the Earth during night-time.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/26/california-sunlight-space-mirrors-satellites\">Continue reading...</a>",
