    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvpccgs3-8tvt",
      "title": "McTominay stars in Napoli draw that leaves Allegri ‘not lucid enough’ to talk",
      "description": "<p><em>Gli Azzurri</em> show positive signs of improvement in seesaw 3-3 draw against a Roma side inspired by Messi-like Matías Soulé</p><p>Scott McTominay was leaving nothing to doubt. He appeared to have scored with a close-range header early in the second half of Napoli’s game at home to Roma, but Pierluigi Gollini clawed the ball out from inside the goal. McTominay got his noggin to the rebound, nudging it back across the line. Roma’s keeper pushed away again, so the Napoli midfielder got to his feet and smashed a shot into the back of the net.</p><p>Just typical. You wait two months for your first goal of the Serie A season, then three show up at once. They only counted for one, of course, but McTominay looked happy enough with that as he ran to thank Matteo Politano for the assist.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/26/scott-mctominay-napoli-roma-serie-a-massimiliano-allegri-not-lucid-enough\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/26/scott-mctominay-napoli-roma-serie-a-massimiliano-allegri-not-lucid-enough",
