      "description": "A solar eclipse recorded more than 2,700 years ago is revealing surprising secrets about Earth&#039;s rotation and the Sun&#039;s ancient behavior. By correcting an eight-kilometer error in the location of an ancient Chinese capital, scientists were able to reconstruct a total solar eclipse that occurred in 709 BCE and obtain more accurate measurements of how fast Earth was spinning at the time.",
