      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvpeg0pk-6c9u",
      "title": "‘Zero-energy companionship’: bizarre hobby takes seed among China’s stressed young adults",
      "description": "<p>Faced with a stagnant jobs market, many are spurning children or pets in favour of ‘raising bricks’</p><p>Young adults in China looking for a cheaper, low-maintenance alternative to having children or pets have found an answer: raising bricks.</p><p>Bricks may not be as cuddly as cats or as life-affirming as human offspring, but they also cost next to nothing. “No cats, no dating, I started raising a brick,” wrote one brick parent on social media.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/zero-energy-companionship-bizarre-hobby-takes-seed-among-chinas-stressed-young-adults\">Continue reading...</a>",
