      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvpccgs3-76y7",
      "title": "Wolff hails Antonelli’s US Grand Prix demolition as the Italian’s ‘best race yet’",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Driver on verge of claiming championship in Mexico</p></li><li><p>‘The drive was exceptional. He outperformed the car’</p></li></ul><p>The Mercedes team principal, Toto Wolff, has paid tribute to his driver Kimi Antonelli, who all but closed out his first Formula One world championship with a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/23/formula-one-kimi-antonelli-mercedes-title-austin-us-grand-prix-texas\">victory at the US Grand Prix</a> that Wolff described as the Italian’s best race yet.</p><p>After the win at the Circuit of the Americas Wolff was also at pains to point out the considerable efforts made by a host of others in bringing the young Italian to having one hand on a record-breaking title.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/26/toto-wolff-hails-kimi-antonelli-us-grand-prix-victory-best-race-yet\">Continue reading...</a>",
