      "quickSummary": [
        "Official verified dispatch from The Guardian World: \"Brexit deal is not good enough for British public, says Andy Burnham\".",
        "Key Context: <p>EU exit has damaged economy and failed to bring promised benefits, says PM, but he rules out big pre-election changes</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/26/an.",
        "Categorized under Current Affairs for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by The Guardian World. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "<p>EU exit has damaged economy and failed to bring promised benefits, says PM, but he rules out big pre-election changes</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/26/andy-burnham-labour-brexit-eu-homelessness-immigration-budget-rosebank-reform-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/26/serbia-vucic-elections-students-bulgaria-france-urkaine-russia-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p><p></p></li></ul><p>Brexit has not “played out” like it was promised to the public, has weakened the economy and the current deal is not good enough, Andy Burnham has said, while ruling out any major changes in the current parliament.</p><p>The prime minister said Britain had ended up with a “harder Brexit than was proposed in the referendum campaign” and it had not helped to control the small boats crisis. Backing the home secretary’s <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/22/energy-secretary-appears-to-u-turn-on-opposition-to-tougher-migration-rules\">tougher immigration rules</a>, he said Brexit had weakened the UK’s ability to control its borders as it could no longer send people back to Europe.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/26/brexit-deal-not-good-enough-andy-burnham\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian World, this report highlights developments in World News.\n\nHeadline: \"Brexit deal is not good enough for British public, says Andy Burnham\"\n\n<p>EU exit has damaged economy and failed to bring promised benefits, says PM, but he rules out big pre-election changes</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/26/andy-burnham-labour-brexit-eu-homelessness-immigration-budget-rosebank-reform-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/26/serbia-vucic-elections-students-bulgaria-france-urkaine-russia-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p><p></p></li></ul><p>Brexit has not “played out” like it was promised to the public, has weakened the economy and the current deal is not good enough, Andy Burnham has said, while ruling out any major changes in the current parliament.</p><p>The prime minister said Britain had ended up with a “harder Brexit than was proposed in the referendum campaign” and it had not helped to control the small boats crisis. Backing the home secretary’s <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/22/energy-secretary-appears-to-u-turn-on-opposition-to-tougher-migration-rules\">tougher immigration rules</a>, he said Brexit had weakened the UK’s ability to control its borders as it could no longer send people back to Europe.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/26/brexit-deal-not-good-enough-andy-burnham\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
