    {
      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvpeg0pp-ziy4",
      "title": "‘It’s collective punishment’: nearly 2,000 Palestinians in Hebron displaced as Israeli forces take over homes",
      "description": "<p>Families forced to flee as Netanyahu tries to prove security credentials after two Israeli soldiers killed days before election</p><p>Hebron, the biggest city in the West Bank, had paid little attention to Israel’s looming elections until it found itself suddenly in the midst of them, a proving ground for Benjamin Netanyahu’s security credentials in the run-up to Tuesday’s vote.</p><p>A <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/israel-soldiers-raze-west-bank-neighbourhood-hebron-families-from-homes\">gun attack on an Israeli military checkpoint</a> on Friday in which two soldiers were killed brought immediate televised visits from Netanyahu and his finance minister, Bezalel Smotrich, whose ruling coalition is <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/oct/25/thousands-rally-against-netanyahu-in-tel-aviv-ahead-of-israeli-elections-video\">narrowly trailing</a> with two days of campaigning left.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/collective-punishment-palestinians-displaced-israeli-forces-take-over-hebron-homes\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/collective-punishment-palestinians-displaced-israeli-forces-take-over-hebron-homes",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/collective-punishment-palestinians-displaced-israeli-forces-take-over-hebron-homes",
      "publisherId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorId": "guardian_world",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian World",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardianworld",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585829365295-ab7cd400c167?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
