      "easySummary": "<p>After a shock defeat in the first round, the incumbent Brazilian president, Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva,<strong> </strong>has turned the election around to win the runoff.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula\">Live blog: latest analysis and reaction</a></p><p>Brazil’s president is elected purely by the popular vote. A winning candidate needs one more vote than 50% of votes cast; there is no role for the parliament and no electoral college.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-2026-live-second-round-results\">Continue reading...</a>",
