      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvpeg0po-k6ct",
      "title": "Serbian leader Aleksandar Vučić ousted by student movement in seismic election",
      "description": "<p>Vučić’s 12-year reign looks to have been ended by record turnout of voters in election provoked by student-led protests</p><p>The long-serving leader of Serbia, Aleksandar Vučić, has conceded defeat, ushering in a seismic political shift after a historic election that saw ​the increasingly authoritarian leader pitted against a student-led movement that had spent two years protesting against his government.</p><p>Vučić pointed to preliminary results that suggested voters had overwhelmingly backed the students, potentially giving them a majority in the country’s 250-seat parliament.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/25/serbian-leader-aleksandar-vucic-concedes-defeat-in-fiercely-contested-parliamentary-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
