    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvpccgs7-8two",
      "title": "Australia’s Rebecca Henderson claims historic race walk world record",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>25-year-old sets new global mark for race walk marathon</p></li><li><p>Rising star slices 19 seconds off previous record despite rain</p></li></ul><p>Rebecca Henderson walked her way into the history books in Japan by becoming the first Australian track and field athlete in a generation to set a senior world record in a championship event.</p><p>The rising 25-year-old from Dandenong set a new global mark for the race walk marathon – the sport’s newest championship event – clocking a remarkable three hours 14 minutes 52 seconds at the All Japan Race Walking meeting on Sunday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/26/australian-rebecca-henderson-breaks-athletics-world-record-race-walk-marathon-japan\">Continue reading...</a>",
