    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvpccgs9-grpu",
      "title": "Terland strikes late as United end Manchester City’s winning start in WSL",
      "description": "<p>At long last, a weakness has been spotted. Finally, the 100% winning start ends for Manchester City, much to the pleasure of Manchester United, who struck late through Elisabeth Terland to claim a point in a well-contested and at times breathless derby.</p><p>Khadija “Bunny” Shaw’s second-half strike – her 91st WSL goal on her 100th appearance in the division – appeared to have settled the game and kept the defending champions top of the table, and it had looked likely to be the same old story, of City finding a way to win a game that was on a knife-edge, because they have the game’s deadliest finisher.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/25/manchester-united-manchester-city-wsl-match-report\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/25/manchester-united-manchester-city-wsl-match-report",
