      "title": "Emirati diplomat who helped deliver aid to Gaza enters UN secretary general race",
      "description": "<p>Lana Nusseibeh has Palestine’s endorsement but faces criticism over UAE’s record on human rights and Sudan</p><p>An Emirati diplomat who as UAE ambassador to the UN helped secure the delivery of humanitarian aid to Gaza has entered the race as a late contender to succeed António Guterres as the world body’s secretary general.</p><p>Lana Nusseibeh, who is of Palestinian heritage, is widely noted for her advocacy of the Palestinian cause and the two-state solution and has won the endorsement of the state of Palestine.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/25/lana-nusseibeh-emirati-diplomat-enters-un-secretary-general-race\">Continue reading...</a>",
