    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvpccgs4-ikky",
      "title": "The WNBA finals are a basketball wonderland – unless you’re part of the Maga machine",
      "description": "<p>The Dream and Valkyries are tied at 2-2 after four absorbing games. Many in America would rather we revisited the national anthem debate</p><p>When Tyler Perry leading lady Crystal Renee took center stage at State Farm Arena to sing the national anthem before the Atlanta Dream’s WNBA finals clash with the Golden State Valkyries on Saturday afternoon, a smattering of photographers, game officials and event security took their familiar places around her as the capacity crowd stood for the flag. The teams, as is now customary, spent that time in their locker rooms. As soon as the lights went back up, the teams returned to the floor to resume their shootarounds. Anyone genuinely invested in the finals would have been unfazed by them briefly stepping away – if they remembered it at all after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/24/golden-state-valkyries-atlanta-dream-game-four-wnba-finals\">the Valkyries’ 67-62 win</a> tied the series at two games apiece. But for many watching the game, basketball is beside the point.</p><p>Seven years ago, Jay-Z declared that the culture had “<a href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/jay-z-defends-his-nfl-deal-i-think-we-have-moved-past-kneeling-192842133.html\">moved past kneeling</a>” and similar national anthem protests, seemingly sounding the death knell for an era of sports activism that had helped raise awareness of racial disparities as a broader social movement gathered force. The line cemented his partnership with the NFL as the league bowed to political pressure to crack down on anthem protests, with other major US sports eventually following the NFL’s lead. But rightwing media and politicians never got the memo. They’re still making sports a battleground for patriotism, with basketball as the war’s chief casualty.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/25/the-wnba-finals-are-a-basketball-wonderland-unless-youre-part-of-the-maga-machine\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/25/the-wnba-finals-are-a-basketball-wonderland-unless-youre-part-of-the-maga-machine",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/25/the-wnba-finals-are-a-basketball-wonderland-unless-youre-part-of-the-maga-machine",
