      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mvpeg0up-dz0l",
      "title": "The BoM’s temperature record keeping is under attack – again. What’s going on? | Temperature Check",
      "description": "<p>An ‘audit’ of the Bureau of Meteorology main dataset for measuring climate change claims it contains ‘widespread errors’. It doesn’t stack up</p><ul><li><p>Want to get this in your inbox when it publishes? <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/mar/10/sign-up-for-the-clear-air-australia-environment-newsletter-with-adam-morton?CMP=cvau_sfl\">Sign up for the Clear Air Australia newsletter here</a></p></li></ul><p></p><p>Australia’s climate has warmed by more than 1.5C since 1910, according to the Bureau of Meteorology’s main long-term temperature data.</p><p>If you were so motivated, you might think if you could discredit this data, then you would undermine the whole climate change story and even – perhaps – the rationale for cutting Australia’s greenhouse gas emissions.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/mar/10/sign-up-for-the-clear-air-australia-environment-newsletter-with-adam-morton?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up to get climate and environment editor Adam Morton’s Clear Air column as a free newsletter</a></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/25/bom-temperature-record-keeping-under-attack-again\">Continue reading...</a>",
