      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mvpeg0uo-3emk",
      "title": "‘Bolso shows all signs of fascism’: the journalist who predicted Brazil’s future – and paid the ultimate price",
      "description": "<p>Dom Phillips warned that Jair Bolsonaro would make life more dangerous for reporters and the Amazon rainforest, and that his sons were even more extreme</p><p>“Bolso shows all signs of fascism, as do his supporters,” the murdered British journalist Dom Phillips told me before his death. “His sons are all more extreme if anything.”</p><p>These words were written in 2018 by the Guardian contributor shortly before the election of the far-right former army captain Jair Bolsonaro as president of Brazil – a prospect that Dom viewed with dread.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/jair-bolsonaro-fascism-journalist-dom-phillips-predicted-brazil-future\">Continue reading...</a>",
