        "Original reporting published by ScienceDaily. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "Scientists discovered that the thick, sticky fluid surrounding glioblastoma tumors can make brain cancer cells smaller, more flexible, and better at invading surrounding tissue. Even more troubling, some of these changes persist after the cells leave the thick fluid, revealing a previously overlooked mechanism that could help this deadly cancer spread.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"Glioblastoma breakthrough reveals how brain cancer cells become more aggressive\"\n\nScientists discovered that the thick, sticky fluid surrounding glioblastoma tumors can make brain cancer cells smaller, more flexible, and better at invading surrounding tissue. Even more troubling, some of these changes persist after the cells leave the thick fluid, revealing a previously overlooked mechanism that could help this deadly cancer spread.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
