      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvpccgs9-5k21",
      "title": "Bavuma’s nine-hour masterpiece was art we risk losing in Test cricket’s great purge | Barney Ronay",
      "description": "<p>T20 franchise cricket is trash sport and killing the five-day game is cultural vandalism. What would Orwell have made of this?</p><p>Have you read George Orwell’s review of Mein Kampf? This might not sound like a grabby reference, or a killer hook for the algorithm. But Hitler is always hot. Hitler is legacy brand. Hitler is eyeballs. Also, it’s just a great review, even more so because it was written at a time when the world didn’t quite know what Hitler was “all about”.</p><p>True, you get a vibe off people. The invasion of France. The ranting, visceral hatred. There were signs, clues, indications that this guy, this guy is <em>not my kind of guy</em>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/23/temba-bavuma-masterpiece-risk-losing-south-africa-test-cricket-purge\">Continue reading...</a>",
