    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvkhuamo-ev54",
      "title": "Caleb Williams outduels friend and rival Drake Maye as Bears beat Patriots",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>New England Patriots 24–30 Chicago Bears</p></li><li><p>Bears QB throws for 308 yards and two TDs</p></li></ul><p>Caleb Williams threw for 308 yards and two touchdowns, and the Chicago Bears cooled off Drake Maye and the New England Patriots with a 30-24 win on Thursday night.</p><p>Williams was 22 of 33 passing in his second game back after being <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/21/bears-say-caleb-williams-is-week-to-week-with-hamstring-injury-and-will-miss-some-time\">sidelined by a hamstring injury</a>. He became the first Bears quarterback to throw for more than 300 yards in consecutive games since Mitch Trubisky had a three-game run in 2018.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/caleb-williams-outduels-friend-and-rival-drake-maye-as-bears-beat-patriots\">Continue reading...</a>",
