      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvkhuamq-zaev",
      "title": "‘The Bird Reich’: Atlanta Falcons roasted over throwback logo with Nazi resemblance",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Retro design features red, white and black stripes</p></li><li><p>Social media users draw Nazi Germany comparisons</p></li><li><p>Falcons’ X post attracts roughly 26m views</p></li></ul><p>Social media erupted in jokes and memes on Thursday after the Atlanta Falcons unveiled a logo that instantly drew comparisons with the imagery of Nazi Germany.</p><p>The logo – posted by the Falcons on the NFL team’s social media channels – shows the team’s old falcon symbol from the 1960s and 1970s, emblazoned on a background of red, white and black stripes.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/atlanta-falcons-throwback-logo-nazi-germany-comparisons-memes\">Continue reading...</a>",
