      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvkhuamr-xpw1",
      "title": "Bruno’s betrayal? ‘Toxic’ Fernandes is symptom of United’s culture of entitlement | Jamie Jackson",
      "description": "<p>Michael Carrick must now deal with more dressing-room unrest after Lisandro Martínez’s attack on the board</p><p>“Toxic”: this is the damning characterisation of Bruno Fernandes from one highly placed Manchester United source after the captain’s incendiary betrayal of Michael Carrick.</p><p>There has surely never been a greater anti-leadership act in United’s history than Fernandes questioning the man who trusts him to unify the dressing room and execute his on-field plan. The Portuguese has proved this faith wrong at the precise moment he was required to step up and exude a defiant togetherness.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/22/bruno-fernandes-betrayal-manchester-united-michael-carrick-culture-of-entitlement\">Continue reading...</a>",
