    {
      "id": "art-guardian_environment-mvpeg0up-5flu",
      "title": "We will make the net-zero transition work for Britain – approving the Jackdaw gasfield is part of the plan | Andy Burnham",
      "description": "<p>Protecting jobs and strengthening energy security in the short term does not mean wavering on Labour’s deep commitment to a cleaner, greener future</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/22/andy-burnham-vows-uk-will-hit-net-zero-targets-despite-jackdaw-gasfield-approval\">Andy Burnham vows UK will hit net zero target despite Jackdaw gasfield approval</a></p></li></ul><p>On Wednesday, the energy secretary, Miatta Fahnbulleh, gave the go-ahead for gas production to begin at the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/21/jackdaw-gasfield-in-north-sea-approved\">Jackdaw gasfield</a> in the North Sea. This has been the subject of fierce debate for many years, with strong views on both sides. I want to explain what the decision means and how it fits with Britain’s climate commitments.</p><p>At a time of acute global instability, it makes sense to responsibly use our resources here at home. Gas from this field will begin heating our homes and powering our businesses this winter. In the longer term, it will significantly strengthen our energy security by <a href=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ad77f4e13c9ff4fd08ed632/20261014_Jackdaw_decision_doc.pdf\">increasing domestic gas production by about 6%</a> and support the UK’s energy supply for more than a decade. Wednesday’s decision will also protect hundreds of jobs in Scotland and add almost £3bn to the UK economy over the lifetime of the project.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/oct/22/net-zero-transition-britain-jackdaw-gasfield-jobs-energy-security-labour\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/oct/22/net-zero-transition-britain-jackdaw-gasfield-jobs-energy-security-labour",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/oct/22/net-zero-transition-britain-jackdaw-gasfield-jobs-energy-security-labour",
      "publisherId": "guardian_environment",
      "creatorId": "guardian_environment",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Environment",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardianeco",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470071459604-3b5ec3a7fe05?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
