    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvkhuamn-gxjh",
      "title": "South Africa beat Boland and weather to force series decider against Australia",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Rabada and Mulder lead hosts to victory in second Test</p></li><li><p>Boland bats for more than three hours as nightwatchman</p></li></ul><p>It took time, it gently frayed nerves, but South Africa sealed the second Test in Gqeberha deep into the final day, clear by an innings and 31 runs, levelling the series with one to play. Although Australia made 295 and got within 28 overs of safety, they did not deserve to save this game, even if Scott Boland and Travis Head did.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/20/australia-on-the-back-foot-as-bavuma-plays-captains-innings-for-south-africa\">Letting South Africa escape</a> from 40 for four to pass 400 was the first offence, then came <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-four-match-report-cricket\">Australia’s capitulation for 99</a> to be forced to follow on. The salvage operation was in waters too deep.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-five-report\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-five-report",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-five-report",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Sport",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardiansport",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Sports",
      "currentAffairsCategory": "Sports",
      "publishDate": "2026-10-22T15:53:38.000Z",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T15:53:38.000Z",
      "firstSeenAt": "2026-10-23T04:52:32.985Z",
      "lastCheckedAt": "2026-10-23T04:53:17.415Z",
      "contentHash": "844b40a0b04f4f42",
      "isUpdate": false,
      "readingTimeMinutes": 5,
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/08135ebcc127f8bae24d5710165de249dde9c0d7/685_0_4105_3284/master/4105.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=fa23c65a9b29748814d1b5dd660595bc&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "originalImageUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/08135ebcc127f8bae24d5710165de249dde9c0d7/685_0_4105_3284/master/4105.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=fa23c65a9b29748814d1b5dd660595bc&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "imageSource": "publisher",
      "imageType": "photo",
      "imageCaption": "Official photograph from The Guardian Sport for \"South Africa beat Boland and weather to force series decider against Australia\"",
      "imageAttribution": "Source: The Guardian Sport",
      "imageValidationStatus": "valid",
      "quickSummary": [
        "Official verified dispatch from The Guardian Sport: \"South Africa beat Boland and weather to force series decider against Australia\".",
        "Key Context: <ul><li><p>Rabada and Mulder lead hosts to victory in second Test</p></li><li><p>Boland bats for more than three hours as nightwatchman</p></li></ul><p>It took time, it gently frayed nerves, but South.",
        "Categorized under Sports for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by The Guardian Sport. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "<ul><li><p>Rabada and Mulder lead hosts to victory in second Test</p></li><li><p>Boland bats for more than three hours as nightwatchman</p></li></ul><p>It took time, it gently frayed nerves, but South Africa sealed the second Test in Gqeberha deep into the final day, clear by an innings and 31 runs, levelling the series with one to play. Although Australia made 295 and got within 28 overs of safety, they did not deserve to save this game, even if Scott Boland and Travis Head did.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/20/australia-on-the-back-foot-as-bavuma-plays-captains-innings-for-south-africa\">Letting South Africa escape</a> from 40 for four to pass 400 was the first offence, then came <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-four-match-report-cricket\">Australia’s capitulation for 99</a> to be forced to follow on. The salvage operation was in waters too deep.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-five-report\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian Sport, this report highlights developments in Sports.\n\nHeadline: \"South Africa beat Boland and weather to force series decider against Australia\"\n\n<ul><li><p>Rabada and Mulder lead hosts to victory in second Test</p></li><li><p>Boland bats for more than three hours as nightwatchman</p></li></ul><p>It took time, it gently frayed nerves, but South Africa sealed the second Test in Gqeberha deep into the final day, clear by an innings and 31 runs, levelling the series with one to play. Although Australia made 295 and got within 28 overs of safety, they did not deserve to save this game, even if Scott Boland and Travis Head did.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/20/australia-on-the-back-foot-as-bavuma-plays-captains-innings-for-south-africa\">Letting South Africa escape</a> from 40 for four to pass 400 was the first offence, then came <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-four-match-report-cricket\">Australia’s capitulation for 99</a> to be forced to follow on. The salvage operation was in waters too deep.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/south-africa-australia-second-test-day-five-report\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
