    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvkhuamw-v3e6",
      "title": "Football Daily | Post-Ferguson worn-out horror show continues at Manchester United",
      "description": "<p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/info/2022/nov/14/football-daily-email-sign-up\"><strong>Sign up now! Sign up now! Sign up now? Sign up now!</strong></a></p><p>We’re in the midst of what the kids call “spooky season” – or, for our fellow fusty old-timers out there, “autumn”. If you’ve been cosying up with a few horror flicks this month, you’ll know nothing good can come from hanging around a lake at this time of year. And so it proved for Manchester United, who endured an early Halloween <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/como-manchester-united-champions-league-match-report\">nightmare on the banks of Lake Como</a> that may have driven a stake through the Michael Carrick era. Hailed as the interim anti-Amorim not so long ago, Carrick has overseen two wins this season, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/aug/30/manchester-united-ipswich-premier-league-match-report\">against Ipswich</a> and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/sep/10/manchester-united-sabah-champions-league-match-report\">Sabah Baku</a>. Como were in Serie D when Carrick won Big Cup with United as a player in 2008 – now, 18 years on, he watched the Italian upstarts dance, twirl and shimmy through the set of training cones he had sent out to represent his storied club.</p><p>Any chance the Independent Football Regulator could <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/manchester-city-david-kogan-independent-football-regulator\">also force the sale</a> of Manchester United while it is at it? – James Marriott.</p><p>Belated birthday greetings to Florent Sinama-Pongolle, a player once described (by Big Website if memory serves) as the only footballer whose surname sounds like an art-house trend – Alan Burgess.</p><p><em><strong>This is an extract from our daily football email … Football Daily. To get the full version,<a href=\"https://preview.gutools.co.uk/info/2016/jan/05/the-fiver-email-sign-up\"> </a><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/info/2022/nov/14/football-daily-email-sign-up\">just visit this page and follow the instructions</a>.</strong></em> </p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/22/football-daily-email-manchester-united\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/22/football-daily-email-manchester-united",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/22/football-daily-email-manchester-united",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Sport",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardiansport",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Sports",
      "currentAffairsCategory": "Sports",
