      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxydb-cb5b",
      "title": "Manchester United bin-fire keeps blazing and Arsenal draw at Bayern: Football Weekly Extra – podcast",
      "description": "<p><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/maxrushden.bsky.social\">Max Rushden</a> is joined by <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/jonathanliew.bsky.social\">Jonathan Liew</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/paul-c-watson.bsky.social\">Paul Watson</a> and <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/archiert1.bsky.social\">Archie Rhind-Tutt</a> to discuss the latest Champions League action</p><p><strong>Max Rushden is joined by <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jonathan-liew\">Jonathan Liew</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/profile/paul-watson\">Paul Watson </a>and Archie Rhind-Tutt to discuss Wednesday night’s Champions League action</strong>.</p><p>On the podcast today: another player questions the hierarchy at Manchester United after they are hammered in Como, but should captain Bruno Fernandes have held his tongue? Michael Carrick may be on the brink, but which top manager would even want this job?</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/audio/2026/oct/22/manchester-united-bin-fire-and-arsenal-draw-in-munich-football-weekly-extra-podcast\">Continue reading...</a>",
