      "id": "art-sciencedaily-mvkhudi9-wied",
      "title": "Millions take fish oil for brain health. A two-year study found no benefit",
      "description": "A surprising two-year clinical trial found that fish oil supplements successfully delivered omega-3s to the brain but failed to improve memory or protect against Alzheimer&#039;s-related brain shrinkage. Researchers suspect that getting these nutrients through a healthy diet may offer benefits that supplements alone cannot provide.",
