        "Original reporting published by The Guardian Sport. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "<p>Austrian’s tactics need adapting to but Forest are in the bottom three and their owner is not the patient type</p><p>Sitting 19th in the Premier League was not the plan for Nottingham Forest after the arrival of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/06/oliver-glasner-confirmed-as-nottingham-forest-head-coach\">a highly acclaimed manager </a>and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/aug/27/liam-delap-signs-nottingham-forest-chelsea-transfer-latest\">a £45m striker </a>to fuel their ambitions. The fates of Oliver Glasner and Liam Delap are intertwined and with the stark stats of zero home goals and a solitary point at the City Ground it is not the dream start they were aiming for.</p><p>As Delap prepares to return to Ipswich, where his career ignited, on Friday night, Forest are remaining calm. There is a desperation to get away from the short-termism that caused so many problems; 12 months ago, they were on their third head coach of a disappointing season. This summer they were ruthless with the removal of Vítor Pereira, who had done a fine job to escape the drop, because they saw an opportunity to upgrade with Glasner, hoping he could transform Forest like he did Crystal Palace.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/22/nottingham-forest-oliver-glasner-time-evangelos-marinakis\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian Sport, this report highlights developments in Sports.\n\nHeadline: \"Nottingham Forest’s false start places early focus on Glasner and Delap\"\n\n<p>Austrian’s tactics need adapting to but Forest are in the bottom three and their owner is not the patient type</p><p>Sitting 19th in the Premier League was not the plan for Nottingham Forest after the arrival of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/06/oliver-glasner-confirmed-as-nottingham-forest-head-coach\">a highly acclaimed manager </a>and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/aug/27/liam-delap-signs-nottingham-forest-chelsea-transfer-latest\">a £45m striker </a>to fuel their ambitions. The fates of Oliver Glasner and Liam Delap are intertwined and with the stark stats of zero home goals and a solitary point at the City Ground it is not the dream start they were aiming for.</p><p>As Delap prepares to return to Ipswich, where his career ignited, on Friday night, Forest are remaining calm. There is a desperation to get away from the short-termism that caused so many problems; 12 months ago, they were on their third head coach of a disappointing season. This summer they were ruthless with the removal of Vítor Pereira, who had done a fine job to escape the drop, because they saw an opportunity to upgrade with Glasner, hoping he could transform Forest like he did Crystal Palace.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/22/nottingham-forest-oliver-glasner-time-evangelos-marinakis\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
