    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxyd6-flbo",
      "title": "Welcome to the trap: swaggering Atlanta Dream turn WNBA finals into a hometown spectacle | Andrew Lawrence",
      "description": "<p>Atlanta’s wounded sports fans know better than to get carried away. But the Dream’s first WNBA finals game in 13 years showed this might finally be a team worth falling for</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/atlanta-dream\">Atlanta Dream</a> were exactly where they wanted to be on Wednesday night, comfortably ensconced inside their downtown arena for Game 3 of the WNBA finals against the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/golden-state-valkyries\">Golden State Valkyries</a>. Kerry Washington, Ludacris and Cam Newton led the courtside celebrity delegation. Quavo and TI headlined the half-time show, while two more hugely popular Atlanta rappers performed during other extended play stoppages – a mini-spectacle that speaks to the city’s deep bench of hip-hop talent.</p><p>But it was the crowd that really made State Farm Arena a house of horrors for Golden State. They didn’t just fill the 17,608-seat venue. They donned matching sky-blue T-shirts and waved rally towels. They sang along with their favorite emcees and lived and died with every point. They were so loud in the first quarter that I couldn’t hear the referee’s whistle from my 100-level press seat. They stayed to the end – well, two minutes from the buzzer anyway (gotta beat traffic) – and, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/angel-reese-atlanta-dream-golden-state-valkyries-wnba-finals\">with the 97-71 win sealed</a> and DJ Khaled’s All I Do Is Win blasting through the arena speakers, serenaded the departing Valkyries with the unofficial Atlanta battle cry: “ATL hoe!”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/atlanta-dream-golden-state-valkyries-wnba-finals-game-three-home-court-advantage\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/atlanta-dream-golden-state-valkyries-wnba-finals-game-three-home-court-advantage",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/atlanta-dream-golden-state-valkyries-wnba-finals-game-three-home-court-advantage",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Sport",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardiansport",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
