      "description": "<p>Video released by Randwick city council shows a whale carcass floating in the water in a Sydney bay, causing the closure of two busy beaches. The whale's decomposed body was found on Thursday morning at Lurline Bay, a rocky cove surrounded by cliffs in Sydney’s eastern suburbs. It’s believed to be a juvenile humpback</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/coogee-maroubra-beaches-closed-whale-carcass\">‘Almost looks fake’: two Sydney beaches closed after whale carcass washes up</a></p></li></ul> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/video/2026/oct/22/whale-carcass-closes-maroubra-and-coogee-beaches-in-sydney-video\">Continue reading...</a>",
