    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxydb-ipz6",
      "title": "‘It doesn’t look good’: Arteta concerned as Saka limps off against Bayern Munich",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>‘A player off with really sharp pain is never good news’</p></li><li><p>Winger forced off 10 minutes into Arsenal’s 2-2 draw</p></li></ul><p>Mikel Arteta made no attempt to conceal his concern over the quad injury that forced Bukayo Saka out of Arsenal’s 2-2 Champions League <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/bayern-munich-arsenal-champions-league-match-report\">draw at Bayern Munich</a>, saying it did not “look good at all”.</p><p>The manager was delighted with the fight that his players showed, Declan Rice earning a deserved point with an 82nd-minute equaliser. Arsenal had led through Eberechi Eze, who came on in the 10th minute for the stricken Saka, before Harry Kane took centre stage. The Bayern striker set up Alphonso Davies for 1-1 before giving his team the lead from the penalty spot.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/champions-league-bayern-munich-arsenal-mikel-arteta-bukayo-saka-injury\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/champions-league-bayern-munich-arsenal-mikel-arteta-bukayo-saka-injury",
