      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxydb-u4ys",
      "title": "Champions League: Silva sparks Real Madrid’s demolition of Leipzig as Lask stun Sporting",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Bernardo Silva opens scoring as Madrid win 4-1</p></li><li><p>Galatasaray sweep past Lille; 10-man Inter edge Shakhtar</p></li></ul><p><strong>Real Madrid</strong> claimed a third Champions League victory in as many games by thrashing <strong>RB Leipzig</strong> 4-1 on Wednesday, with Kylian Mbappé and Yan Diomande among the goals for José Mourinho’s side.</p><p>Bernardo Silva opened the scoring for Madrid from close range towards the end of a tight first half, with Arda Guler doubling the record 15-time European champions’ advantage soon after the interval.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/champions-league-roundup-real-madrid-leipzig-inter-shakhtar-sporting-lask-brugge-lens-betis-feyenoord\">Continue reading...</a>",
