    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxyd5-1ckc",
      "title": "‘Angry’ Carrick on the brink as Fernandes hits out at Manchester United tactics",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Manager apologises to fans after 4-1 defeat in Como</p></li><li><p>Captain criticises ‘decision from the staff’ not to press</p></li></ul><p>Michael Carrick’s future as Manchester United manager is in the balance after a humiliating 4-1 Champions League defeat by Como on Wednesday night.</p><p>Before Bournemouth’s visit to Old Trafford on Sunday his future may be discussed by Jason Wilcox, the director of football, Omar Berrada, the chief executive, and Sir Jim Ratcliffe, the co-owner who controls sporting policy.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/michael-carrick-bruno-fernandes-manchester-united-como-champions-league\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/michael-carrick-bruno-fernandes-manchester-united-como-champions-league",
