      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxyd8-fxsf",
      "title": "Jimmy Anderson set to retire from cricket as Lancashire opt against renewing contract",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>England bowler may have played last game at age 44</p></li><li><p>Lancashire tell Anderson he does not fit their plans</p><p></p><p></p></li></ul><p>Jimmy Anderson is expected to call time on his remarkable career at the age of 44 after being told his contract at Lancashire will not be renewed for next season.</p><p>A change of direction is under way at Old Trafford after the club finished second-bottom of Division Two in the County Championship this year and failed to get out of the group stages in both men’s white-ball competitions.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/jimmy-anderson-set-to-retire-from-cricket-lancashire-contract\">Continue reading...</a>",
