    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxyd8-95wa",
      "title": "Maro Itoje seals England future by agreeing new deal with Saracens",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Captain will resist lure of big-money move to France</p></li><li><p>‘Maro is everything we want at the club – a brilliant leader’</p></li></ul><p>Maro Itoje has reaffirmed his long‑term commitment to England, rejecting interest from France by agreeing a new deal with Saracens.</p><p>Itoje’s existing deal, signed in 2024, was due to expire after the World Cup next year but he has agreed terms with his club despite interest from Top 14 sides. A move to either Perpignan or Bordeaux had been mooted but the 31-year-old is to commit his future to the club he first represented in 2013 with a new deal, believed to be until 2029.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/maro-itoje-england-saracens-new-deal-rugby\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/maro-itoje-england-saracens-new-deal-rugby",
