      "id": "art-mongabay-mvjly0sd-35q4",
      "title": "Seabird guano and native trees keep islands above rising seas: Study",
      "description": "Low-lying tropical atoll islands appear remarkably vulnerable to climate change. But when shrouded with native forests and with abundant seabird populations, these islands may keep up with rising sea levels, a new study finds. Seabirds act as biological pumps, moving nutrients from feeding areas in the open ocean to roosting and nesting areas on land [&#8230;]",
