    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxyde-7u4u",
      "title": "Football Daily | Champions League drama galore – so why do we feel hollow?",
      "description": "<p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/info/2022/nov/14/football-daily-email-sign-up\"><strong>Sign up now! Sign up now! Sign up now? Sign up now!</strong></a></p><p>Now then, which one of you hipsters decided to put Porto 0-1 PSV on? Oh dear. This was another night of Bigger Cup at its Bigliest self, comebacks everywhere, 40 goals in nine games, six of those in a best-v-best clash as <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/20/paris-saint-germain-psg-barcelona-champions-league-match-report\">Paris Saint-Germain rallied late</a> against Barcelona. Even in defeat, Lamine Yamal found space to decorate the room with a ludicrous toe-poke equaliser, and there was a wholesome tale in Italy as Scott McTominay <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/20/champions-league-roundup-mctominay-scores-twice-on-return-from-heart-surgery\">scored twice for Napoli</a> in their 4-3 win against Bodø/Glimt. These were his first strikes since returning from heart surgery, taking his tally at the club to 29 goals in 86 appearances. No wonder <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/20/erik-ten-hag-accuses-cristiano-ronaldo-of-letting-down-manchester-united\">Erik ten Hag was peeved</a> with his bosses at Manchester United for shipping the midfielder off to Naples.</p><p>One has to admire the courage of Erik ten Hag, speaking out on Man United’s ‘toxic culture’ [yesterday’s Football Daily, full email edition]. I broke out in a cold sweat reading about how they ‘give power to the players’. The stuff of nightmares, really” – Rowan Sweeney.</p><p>Roberto De Zerbi wants Spurs to be a family (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/20/tottenham-hotspur-win-football-daily-newsletter\">yesterday’s Football Daily</a>)? And he thinks playing for or with a family will avoid relegation? Well, I have this uncle. He’s called Weird Uncle Fiver (now there’s a throwback – Football Daily Ed), and he loves to [snip – Football Daily lawyers, and time-travelling pedants]” – Mike Wilner.</p><p><em><strong>This is an extract from our daily football email … Football Daily. To get the full version,<a href=\"https://preview.gutools.co.uk/info/2016/jan/05/the-fiver-email-sign-up\"> </a><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/info/2022/nov/14/football-daily-email-sign-up\">just visit this page and follow the instructions</a>.</strong></em> </p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/champions-league-goals-football-daily-newsletter\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/champions-league-goals-football-daily-newsletter",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/21/champions-league-goals-football-daily-newsletter",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Sport",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardiansport",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Sports",
