    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxyda-ktpx",
      "title": "Austin GP is about much more than potential for Antonelli’s first F1 world title | Giles Richards",
      "description": "<p>Young driver’s maiden championship is all but secured but Mercedes upgrades will inform next year’s run to the line</p><p>There is nothing quite like a potential title decider to bring the fiercest of spotlights to bear as doubtless Kimi Antonelli will discover when he attempts to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/11/antonelli-one-win-from-title-after-verstappen-wins-singapore-f1-gp\">seal his first championship</a> at the United States Grand Prix this weekend.</p><p>For the young Italian the goal is straightforward and the culmination of a childhood dream. However, for his Mercedes team there will be scrutiny over performance in Austin that has significant implications going into next season.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/austin-gp-about-much-more-than-potential-kimi-antonelli-first-f1-world-title\">Continue reading...</a>",
