      "easySummary": "<p>All-rounder and ‘the best teammate you could wish for’ has seen profound change since his first-class debut in 2006</p><p>The Spin this week comes from York, where Chris Woakes and I sat down on Monday evening to discuss his new autobiography, The Wizard. There were just shy of 400 international wickets on stage, not a single one mine, and an audience that happened to include one of his old teachers.</p><p>It turns out a seemingly clean-cut cricketer was something of a rebel back in the day, with Mr Wager reminding Chris of the time he feigned illness to bunk off school for a long weekend in Newquay with his mates. A bit like <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/26/warwickshire-clinch-county-championship-title-with-victory-over-leicestershire\">Warwickshire’s title win this year</a> that anecdote came too late, frustratingly, for the hardback edition.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/the-spin-cricket-book-chris-woakes-nicest-man-in-cricket\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian Sport, this report highlights developments in Sports.\n\nHeadline: \"The Spin | Writing a book with Chris Woakes showed the inner steel of the nicest man in cricket\"\n\n<p>All-rounder and ‘the best teammate you could wish for’ has seen profound change since his first-class debut in 2006</p><p>The Spin this week comes from York, where Chris Woakes and I sat down on Monday evening to discuss his new autobiography, The Wizard. There were just shy of 400 international wickets on stage, not a single one mine, and an audience that happened to include one of his old teachers.</p><p>It turns out a seemingly clean-cut cricketer was something of a rebel back in the day, with Mr Wager reminding Chris of the time he feigned illness to bunk off school for a long weekend in Newquay with his mates. A bit like <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/26/warwickshire-clinch-county-championship-title-with-victory-over-leicestershire\">Warwickshire’s title win this year</a> that anecdote came too late, frustratingly, for the hardback edition.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/21/the-spin-cricket-book-chris-woakes-nicest-man-in-cricket\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
