      "id": "art-guardian_world-mvpeg0pr-1l6o",
      "title": "Billionaire Mukesh Ambani launches India’s biggest-ever IPO",
      "description": "<p>Low-cost broadband provider Jio Platforms aims for £81bn valuation when it floats on the stock market on Wednesday</p><p>India’s second-richest man, Mukesh Ambani, is launching what could be the country’s biggest-ever initial public offering (IPO), despite a stock market downturn.</p><p>Mumbai-based Jio Platforms, a telecoms company backed by Meta Platforms and Google, is hoping to raise up to 302bn rupees (£2.4bn) and is targeting a 10.3tn rupees valuation when it floats on the stock market from Wednesday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/20/mukesh-ambani-jio-platforms-ipo-india-stock-market\">Continue reading...</a>",
