    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxydd-lfsu",
      "title": "Dwight Yorke: ‘I’m not a kid trying to get into management – I’m a manager’",
      "description": "<p>Ghana may soon come calling for Trinidad and Tobago’s former captain and manager, who is proud of his CV since his days as a Premier League striker</p><p>Dwight Yorke wants you to stop calling him a former player. “I’m not a kid trying to get into management for the first time,” he says from his home in Dubai. “I’ve done that and I want that message to come across clearly.”</p><p>The message has a deadline. Carlos Queiroz left his job as Ghana head coach on 1 October and the Ghana Football Association is searching for his successor. Yorke is among the names under consideration, along with Pape Thiaw, Aliou Cissé and Walid Regragui, the former Morocco head coach, according to Ghanaian media.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/20/dwight-yorke-interview-manager-ghana-trinidad-and-tobago\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/20/dwight-yorke-interview-manager-ghana-trinidad-and-tobago",
