      "quickSummary": [
        "Official verified dispatch from ScienceDaily: \"Scientists uncover 3 key brain pathways linked to lasting depression relief\".",
        "Key Context: Researchers have uncovered three brain pathways linked to lasting improvements in people receiving deep brain stimulation for severe, treatment-resistant depression. They also discovered that patients.",
        "Categorized under Health for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by ScienceDaily. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "Researchers have uncovered three brain pathways linked to lasting improvements in people receiving deep brain stimulation for severe, treatment-resistant depression. They also discovered that patients who failed to improve after two years shared a striking pattern: insufficient stimulation of a crucial brain connection. The findings suggest that millimeters in electrode placement could make a major difference in treatment outcomes.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"Scientists uncover 3 key brain pathways linked to lasting depression relief\"\n\nResearchers have uncovered three brain pathways linked to lasting improvements in people receiving deep brain stimulation for severe, treatment-resistant depression. They also discovered that patients who failed to improve after two years shared a striking pattern: insufficient stimulation of a crucial brain connection. The findings suggest that millimeters in electrode placement could make a major difference in treatment outcomes.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
