      "quickSummary": [
        "Official verified dispatch from ScienceDaily: \"Scientists discover that male and female skin play by different rules\".",
        "Key Context: Scientists have uncovered a surprising difference in how male and female skin repairs and renews itself. By tracking individual skin stem cells in living mice for five months, researchers discovered t.",
        "Categorized under Health for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by ScienceDaily. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "Scientists have uncovered a surprising difference in how male and female skin repairs and renews itself. By tracking individual skin stem cells in living mice for five months, researchers discovered that female cells work together in a highly coordinated way, while male cells operate more independently. This synchronization, driven by sex hormones, helps explain why wounds heal faster in female mice, especially during the first few days.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"Scientists discover that male and female skin play by different rules\"\n\nScientists have uncovered a surprising difference in how male and female skin repairs and renews itself. By tracking individual skin stem cells in living mice for five months, researchers discovered that female cells work together in a highly coordinated way, while male cells operate more independently. This synchronization, driven by sex hormones, helps explain why wounds heal faster in female mice, especially during the first few days.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
