      "easySummary": "NASA’s James Webb Space Telescope has revealed that a turbulent world 20 light-years away has a surprisingly orderly weather system, with three recurring atmospheric states driven by temperature changes and shifting clouds. The breakthrough gives scientists a powerful new tool for uncovering weather patterns on distant worlds and understanding the conditions that shape their atmospheres.",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by ScienceDaily, this report highlights developments in Science & Technology.\n\nHeadline: \"NASA’s Webb reveals the wild weather of a mysterious world 20 light-years away\"\n\nNASA’s James Webb Space Telescope has revealed that a turbulent world 20 light-years away has a surprisingly orderly weather system, with three recurring atmospheric states driven by temperature changes and shifting clouds. The breakthrough gives scientists a powerful new tool for uncovering weather patterns on distant worlds and understanding the conditions that shape their atmospheres.\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
