      "id": "art-sciencedaily-mvjly0p2-ze41",
      "title": "James Webb reveals a strange bulge in an alien planet&#039;s atmosphere",
      "description": "Astronomers using the James Webb Space Telescope have discovered that a distant alien planet&#039;s atmosphere is surprisingly lopsided. Located 1,300 light-years away, the scorching gas giant WASP-17b experiences powerful winds that redistribute heat, causing one side of its atmosphere to bulge outward. A groundbreaking new mapping technique revealed these hidden distortions, confirming predictions about how extreme temperatures and winds shape alien worlds.",
