    {
      "id": "art-the_guardian_sport-mvjlxyde-g2j7",
      "title": "Christian Horner: ‘Not all teams act that way. You don’t see the same brutality as when I left’",
      "description": "<p>The 52-year-old reflects on the pain of being sacked after two decades turning Red Bull into an F1 powerhouse, questioning his purpose in life and dealing with panic attacks</p><p>Christian Horner should be in steamy Singapore, preparing for another grand prix victory, but here he is, at home on an autumnal morning in genteel Highgate as his wife, Geri Halliwell-Horner, welcomes me with a cheerful hug. Horner smiles as the former Spice Girl produces an impressive imitation of my South African accent which echoes her old headteacher at Watford Girls.</p><p>After the most controversial man in the recent history of Formula One says hello, Halliwell-Horner and I discuss the fact that my two daughters also went to her school and that one of their history textbooks had her name printed on the inside page – while the ex-Ginger Spice talks about gritty old Watford, grammar school education and Nelson Mandela.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/12/christian-horner-red-bull-formula-one\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/12/christian-horner-red-bull-formula-one",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/12/christian-horner-red-bull-formula-one",
      "publisherId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorId": "the_guardian_sport",
      "creatorName": "The Guardian Sport",
      "creatorHandle": "@guardiansport",
      "creatorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461896836934-ffe607ba8211?w=120&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "platform": "news",
      "category": "Sports",
      "currentAffairsCategory": "Sports",
      "publishDate": "2026-10-12T18:00:01.000Z",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-12T18:00:01.000Z",
      "firstSeenAt": "2026-10-22T13:59:36.003Z",
      "lastCheckedAt": "2026-10-22T13:59:36.003Z",
      "contentHash": "d0198c3fa996c19e",
      "isUpdate": false,
      "readingTimeMinutes": 5,
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/dfe042e90dc3ab6ab05b154bd2f44371cfb4d894/683_0_6827_5464/master/6827.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=10dbdcc4374dda2f06d3ea8d27f5297f&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "originalImageUrl": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/dfe042e90dc3ab6ab05b154bd2f44371cfb4d894/683_0_6827_5464/master/6827.jpg?width=1000&amp%3Bquality=85&amp%3Bauto=format&amp%3Bfit=max&amp%3Bs=10dbdcc4374dda2f06d3ea8d27f5297f&quality=85&auto=format&fit=max",
      "imageSource": "publisher",
      "imageType": "photo",
      "imageCaption": "Official photograph from The Guardian Sport for \"Christian Horner: ‘Not all teams act that way. You don’t see the same brutality as when I left’\"",
      "imageAttribution": "Source: The Guardian Sport",
      "imageValidationStatus": "valid",
      "quickSummary": [
        "Official verified dispatch from The Guardian Sport: \"Christian Horner: ‘Not all teams act that way. You don’t see the same brutality as when I left’\".",
        "Key Context: <p>The 52-year-old reflects on the pain of being sacked after two decades turning Red Bull into an F1 powerhouse, questioning his purpose in life and dealing with panic attacks</p><p>Christian Horner .",
        "Categorized under Sports for global monitoring and reference.",
        "Original reporting published by The Guardian Sport. Direct canonical dispatch linked."
      ],
      "easySummary": "<p>The 52-year-old reflects on the pain of being sacked after two decades turning Red Bull into an F1 powerhouse, questioning his purpose in life and dealing with panic attacks</p><p>Christian Horner should be in steamy Singapore, preparing for another grand prix victory, but here he is, at home on an autumnal morning in genteel Highgate as his wife, Geri Halliwell-Horner, welcomes me with a cheerful hug. Horner smiles as the former Spice Girl produces an impressive imitation of my South African accent which echoes her old headteacher at Watford Girls.</p><p>After the most controversial man in the recent history of Formula One says hello, Halliwell-Horner and I discuss the fact that my two daughters also went to her school and that one of their history textbooks had her name printed on the inside page – while the ex-Ginger Spice talks about gritty old Watford, grammar school education and Nelson Mandela.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/12/christian-horner-red-bull-formula-one\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "detailedSummary": "Published by The Guardian Sport, this report highlights developments in Sports.\n\nHeadline: \"Christian Horner: ‘Not all teams act that way. You don’t see the same brutality as when I left’\"\n\n<p>The 52-year-old reflects on the pain of being sacked after two decades turning Red Bull into an F1 powerhouse, questioning his purpose in life and dealing with panic attacks</p><p>Christian Horner should be in steamy Singapore, preparing for another grand prix victory, but here he is, at home on an autumnal morning in genteel Highgate as his wife, Geri Halliwell-Horner, welcomes me with a cheerful hug. Horner smiles as the former Spice Girl produces an impressive imitation of my South African accent which echoes her old headteacher at Watford Girls.</p><p>After the most controversial man in the recent history of Formula One says hello, Halliwell-Horner and I discuss the fact that my two daughters also went to her school and that one of their history textbooks had her name printed on the inside page – while the ex-Ginger Spice talks about gritty old Watford, grammar school education and Nelson Mandela.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/12/christian-horner-red-bull-formula-one\">Continue reading...</a>\n\nThe World Ledger maintains strict source attribution and preserves the publisher's original journalism without automated hallucination.",
      "keyFacts": {
